wers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fi3ework","id":12322740,"login":"fi3ework","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzIyNzQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/7a8ff1690b7eebbc65725e698ccfeba584c6e5b7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T05:04:25Z","email":"fi3ework@gmail.com","name":"Max"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T05:04:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(storybook-sync): slice upstream ranges by git ref instead of date (#585)\n\n* refactor(storybook-sync): slice upstream ranges by git ref instead of date\n\nEvery sync run now covers ANCHOR..TARGET where both ends are git refs\n(usually tags, sometimes bare shas) reachable from upstream `next`. TARGET\nis always user-specified; ANCHOR is recovered from a machine-readable\n`<!-- storybook-sync: target=<sha> -->` marker in the previous report\nissue instead of grepping the human-readable Range line, which picked the\nwrong sha on the latest report.\n\nScript changes:\n- drop --days/--since/--until; range modes require --from and --to\n- --from is inclusive (`TO --not FROM^@`), so callers no longer append `^`\n- --resolve validates refs (exist, reachable from origin/next) and prints\n  SHA<TAB>LABEL; range queries validate through the same helper\n- fetch only `origin next` plus tags\n\n* fix(storybook-sync): reject reversed ranges and resolve branches via origin\n\n- refuse a --to that is not a descendant of --from, so a target older than\n  the anchor cannot produce an empty report that moves the marker backward\n- resolve bare branch names as origin/<branch>; the local `next` created by\n  the initial clone is never advanced by the fetch\n\n* docs(storybook-sync): make anchor recovery observable and define placeholders\n\nFound by a dry run of the workflow:\n- the anchor query now prints the issue number even when the marker is\n  missing, so \"no prior report\" and \"report predates the marker\" are\n  distinguishable instead of both reading as an empty result\n- assign TARGET and ANCHOR explicitly before they are dereferenced\n- define `<skill-dir>` once and note that shell state does not persist\n  between tool calls\n- the Range label shapes were examples, not an exhaustive list\n\n* docs(storybook-sync): say \"no parseable marker\" instead of \"predates the marker\"\n\nAn edited or malformed marker line yields the same empty result, so the\noutcome must not be reported as a fact about report history.\n\n* docs(storybook-sync): skip anchor recovery when the user names a start ref\n\nFollowed literally, the old order queried GitHub and then discarded the\nresult whenever the user supplied both ends of the range.\n\n* feat(storybook-sync): exclusive anchor and triage rules for ported or diverged changes\n\n- the anchor is the last commit the previous report covered, so the range\n  is now git-native ANCHOR..TARGET and no longer re-triages it every run\n- new skip grounds: change already present in the local counterpart\n  (cite file:line), and a still-valid intentional divergence re-verified\n  against current local code; a stale divergence is classified normally\n  and flagged for update in the port PR\n- explain manifest `local: null` entries and `ignoredUpstreamFiles`\n- test-only commits map to the counterpart of the file under test\n- supersede chains are judged by their end state, like revert chains\n\n* docs(storybook-sync): close the wording gaps found by the fourth dry run\n\n- \"skip step 3\" meant item 3 of the same list, not the analysis step\n- snippets are bash; REPORT_NAME must be re-inlined in steps 4 and 5\n- read the end state at TARGET_SHA when a chain''s diffs disagree\n- give the manifest lookup command; divergence re-verification may need\n  the installed loader or plugin\n- \"superseded by a later commit\" is an explicit skip ground with a\n  required back-reference\n- the `since #N` label replaces only the plain label, never the links\n- define \"Needs attention\" as high + medium + low\n\n* fix(storybook-sync): fetch all remote branches and keep report filenames slash-free\n\n- the resolver accepts branch names, so the fetch must refresh every\n  remote-tracking branch, not only origin/next\n- a label such as origin/next would otherwise turn the report path into a\n  nonexistent subdirectory","tree":{"sha":"e3606a8d6c8cd57ee9d1dacc9a48913a7bd2271d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/trees/e3606a8d6c8cd57ee9d1dacc9a48913a7bd2271d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/commits/7a8ff1690b7eebbc65725e698ccfeba584c6e5b7","verification":{"payload":"tree e3606a8d6c8cd57ee9d1dacc9a48913a7bd2271d\nparent 7649965459d201e0ef69048a3304bc10df9a2121\nauthor Max <fi3ework@gmail.com> 1789967065 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789967065 +0800\n\nrefactor(storybook-sync): slice upstream ranges by git ref instead of date (#585)\n\n* refactor(storybook-sync): slice upstream ranges by git ref instead of date\n\nEvery sync run now covers ANCHOR..TARGET where both ends are git refs\n(usually tags, sometimes bare shas) reachable from upstream `next`. TARGET\nis always user-specified; ANCHOR is recovered from a machine-readable\n`<!-- storybook-sync: target=<sha> -->` marker in the previous report\nissue instead of grepping the human-readable Range line, which picked the\nwrong sha on the latest report.\n\nScript changes:\n- drop --days/--since/--until; range modes require --from and --to\n- --from is inclusive (`TO --not FROM^@`), so callers no longer append `^`\n- --resolve validates refs (exist, reachable from origin/next) and prints\n  SHA<TAB>LABEL; range queries validate through the same helper\n- fetch only `origin next` plus tags\n\n* fix(storybook-sync): reject reversed ranges and resolve branches via origin\n\n- refuse a --to that is not a descendant of --from, so a target older than\n  the anchor cannot produce an empty report that moves the marker backward\n- resolve bare branch names as origin/<branch>; the local `next` created by\n  the initial clone is never advanced by the fetch\n\n* docs(storybook-sync): make anchor recovery observable and define placeholders\n\nFound by a dry run of the workflow:\n- the anchor query now prints the issue number even when the marker is\n  missing, so \"no prior report\" and \"report predates the marker\" are\n  distinguishable instead of both reading as an empty result\n- assign TARGET and ANCHOR explicitly before they are dereferenced\n- define `<skill-dir>` once and note that shell state does not persist\n  between tool calls\n- the Range label shapes were examples, not an exhaustive list\n\n* docs(storybook-sync): say \"no parseable marker\" instead of \"predates the marker\"\n\nAn edited or malformed marker line yields the same empty result, so the\noutcome must not be reported as a fact about report history.\n\n* docs(storybook-sync): skip anchor recovery when the user names a start ref\n\nFollowed literally, the old order queried GitHub and then discarded the\nresult whenever the user supplied both ends of the range.\n\n* feat(storybook-sync): exclusive anchor and triage rules for ported or diverged changes\n\n- the anchor is the last commit the previous report covered, so the range\n  is now git-native ANCHOR..TARGET and no longer re-triages it every run\n- new skip grounds: change already present in the local counterpart\n  (cite file:line), and a still-valid intentional divergence re-verified\n  against current local code; a stale divergence is classified normally\n  and flagged for update in the port PR\n- explain manifest `local: null` entries and `ignoredUpstreamFiles`\n- test-only commits map to the counterpart of the file under test\n- supersede chains are judged by their end state, like revert chains\n\n* docs(storybook-sync): close the wording gaps found by the fourth dry run\n\n- \"skip step 3\" meant item 3 of the same list, not the analysis step\n- snippets are bash; REPORT_NAME must be re-inlined in steps 4 and 5\n- read the end state at TARGET_SHA when a chain''s diffs disagree\n- give the manifest lookup command; divergence re-verification may need\n  the installed loader or plugin\n- \"superseded by a later commit\" is an explicit skip ground with a\n  required back-reference\n- the `since #N` label replaces only the plain label, never the links\n- define \"Needs attention\" as high + medium + low\n\n* fix(storybook-sync): fetch all remote branches and keep report filenames slash-free\n\n- the resolver accepts branch names, so the fetch must refresh every\n  remote-tracking branch, not only origin/next\n- a label such as origin/next would otherwise turn the report path into a\n  nonexistent subdirectory","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsLrZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWrUQAAIrZq9RtD6wZuU5qcIlgHBu\n9FEMr8V85jWZTfJx0A4hOiamSICSnCaqzfVZqmys/OW7e7bGQYgy/qk7OcO52tcM\noof8I73eSQB3OHlDAnXmtszlw4epgZPM9BTyQfeLE55tFnwKqutNy6wyQuMoW003\nIoACfD7LejoqO88qZxbldon8BWsxk85s8DYU79jKrHPLqDVNbushD7ojwmx+Tfjo\nZi4P2JY9/57zEA9519pwOpL/tn20uy0CdIw2lOI3ZMlrmmREVONr6iNn31Jvli1/\n6fb92rQTwfKmKzoeCTcuHz78BT9gWXGPW0WxvCQ3blhGZG3QACe9BBS8SscUgd/U\nbxu2WwRKmYK+HONNCThwZrM/eUQYrMhp17a8xPUL2nNuLDVwV0Vd65WT9b7ZVbmN\ngTsefiW/pdIkGPXKAvd1Rhdek