:0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T08:12:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(framework-react): use upstream getTsconfigPathsBaseDir (#581)\n\nStorybook 10.6.0, the minimum supported peer, exports\ngetTsconfigPathsBaseDir from storybook/internal/common. Import it\nthere instead of the local backport.\n\n- Delete loaders/tsconfig-paths.ts and its unit tests.\n- Drop the strip-json-comments dependency, used only by the backport.\n- Remove the two getReactDocgenImporter stub-identity tests (\"should\n  map the request\", \"should not map the request...\") as mirror tests.\n  The referenced-tsconfig integration test now covers the mapping path\n  with a fixture that inherits paths from an extended base config\n  without baseUrl.\n\nUpstream: storybookjs/storybook@aa5790bb3484153ce3e9fe409e0ab516c2853e58\nRefs #544","tree":{"sha":"28ce0b3afe174116f31e69244a1be08a29209e67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/trees/28ce0b3afe174116f31e69244a1be08a29209e67"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/commits/6f612a819e811f90d143fbd2a7b62f1f8aa51c77","verification":{"payload":"tree 28ce0b3afe174116f31e69244a1be08a29209e67\nparent 8e7425261266c7ba573da8cabf748b3bc57dabe4\nauthor Max <fi3ework@gmail.com> 1789719154 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789719154 +0000\n\nrefactor(framework-react): use upstream getTsconfigPathsBaseDir (#581)\n\nStorybook 10.6.0, the minimum supported peer, exports\ngetTsconfigPathsBaseDir from storybook/internal/common. Import it\nthere instead of the local backport.\n\n- Delete loaders/tsconfig-paths.ts and its unit tests.\n- Drop the strip-json-comments dependency, used only by the backport.\n- Remove the two getReactDocgenImporter stub-identity tests (\"should\n  map the request\", \"should not map the request...\") as mirror tests.\n  The referenced-tsconfig integration test now covers the mapping path\n  with a fixture that inherits paths from an extended base config\n  without baseUrl.\n\nUpstream: storybookjs/storybook@aa5790bb3484153ce3e9fe409e0ab516c2853e58\nRefs #544","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrPJyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAflEQADU8Z0h4MsGRZo7Rcwcdm8A2\nEESISL4ZfjU5+rhstRHyQVYrebG5UVxi1l1GJfQb0OD8mX96AQez+AzkuYJgK49O\nD2KImmW61DSX3V/I+RzTSIUkWRdXI2ptAlNEgHC2Wi2X0tFItm8hvHcdo269sjYl\n4vlNyDTOM1DfS1djl+PL0If96rGbKPvXEnsXI9YDFxvoUGClx562+ZogCt3JNGqU\n81LbfIik5kJ2QVE4RAwZbDxSIPYuFRI7D5O6zCb3l12MKc+jdDQWcMWU93FHvGmo\nnIw8DEwZhTNwDaS4Ex4+zu0rdp1j2fZEkYBN/uxFbAasjguH9zgKYyUSAzdDKJxB\nryyLyVtpp9iIrjb3xanTYYGABxzCsCEO9cINIVHM0VaREm+cKslTgXez7izmQUTL\nVNrtEWbjVSlViSs5/Kgah3ZbL2luEVw5AlaMTxjYePHfi8KuLJnjUoQ2F6Pmc+9s\n4BgwGr7YLlNhmf3U4HKDkcp7URAGCYaX196V/VYDVNuro/J9yu/a7JgbgGEtOcDN\nE13RaZXD/29reS+XOBbC/n0UurR+9Y0qCoOu7+3VNEmUwL5XFeU7+l2jLy23sHwR\nEIcP6lHxuZh74ab4/iU3gOCIXC/hwEoHjGkgCUyuCuriO+sJQlhR3hN2Yn+WgiOd\nM4NMeYHhs4ABUiydLxQp\n=a7hk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T08:12:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commit/6f612a819e811f90d143fbd2a7b62f1f8aa51c77","node_id":"C_kwDOL8RLndoAKDZmNjEyYTgxOWU4MTFmOTBkMTQzZmJkMmE3YjYyZjFmOGFhNTFjNzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commit/8e7425261266c7ba573da8cabf748b3bc57dabe4","sha":"8e7425261266c7ba573da8cabf748b3bc57dabe4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/8e7425261266c7ba573da8cabf748b3bc57dabe4"}],"sha":"6f612a819e811f90d143fbd2a7b62f1f8aa51c77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/6f612a819e811f90d143fbd2a7b62f1f8aa51c77"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/2740?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/renovate","id":29139614,"login":"renovate[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90MjkxMzk2MTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/8e7425261266c7ba573da8cabf748b3bc57dabe4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T07:36:56Z","email":"29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"renovate[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T07:36:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(deps): update all non-major dependencies (#541)\n\n* chore(deps): update all non-major dependencies\n\n* fix(sandbox): drop unused ts-expect-error after modern.js 3.9 bump\n\n* feat(rsbuild-plugin-react-native-web): support reanimated 4 webUtils imports\n\nreanimated 4 ships js-reanimated/webUtils.js as plain ESM that bare-imports\nreact-native-web/dist/cjs/... without declaring react-native-web as a\ndependency, so under pnpm''s isolated node_modules the specifiers cannot be\nresolved from within reanimated''s virtual store. Extend the existing\nwebUtils transform to rewrite those specifiers to absolute paths via\nresolveModule (framework-react-native-web already passes reactNativeWebPath),\nfalling back to untouched code when no resolver is available or throws. The\n3.x webUtils.web.js export-let/try/require transform is unchanged.\n\nAlso upgrade the react-native-web sandbox to react-native-reanimated\n^3.19.5 -> ^4.6.0 (react-native-worklets ^0.12.2). This additionally removes\nthe @babel/types 8.x phantom-dependency crash of reanimated 3''s Babel plugin,\nwhich loaded an undeclared hoisted @babel/types 8.0.4 and threw\n\"NumericLiterals must be non-negative finite numbers\"; worklets 0.12 declares\n@babel/types ^7 so the plugin now resolves a safe 7.x copy.\n\n* revert(rsbuild-plugin-react-native-web): drop reanimated 4 webUtils import rewrite\n\nThe rewrite patched around react-native-reanimated''s undeclared\nreact-native-web dependency at build time; a pnpm-workspace.yaml\nhoistPattern entry now covers it for every bundler instead.\n\n* chore: hoist react-native-web for reanimated 4 and drop worklets babel hoists\n\nreact-native-reanimated 4''s js-reanimated/webUtils.js imports\nreact-native-web/dist/cjs/... without declaring react-native-web as a\ndependency. pnpm''s default hoistPattern [''*''] covers this, but this repo\nrestricts hoistPattern, so add react-native-web to it. Conversely,\nreact-native-worklets 0.12 declares @babel/types, @babel/generator and\n@babel/traverse in its own dependencies, so those hoist entries are no\nlonger needed and are removed.\n\nAlso document the pnpm hoisting requirement in the react-native-web\nframework guide (en + zh).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: fi3ework <fi3ework@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"825c8aae02e6487f29862c817b3622cabbb43741","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/trees/825c8aae02e6487f29862c817b3622cabbb43741"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/commits/8e7425261266c7ba573da8cabf748b3bc57dabe4","verification":{"payload":"tree 825c8aae02e6487f29862c817b3622cabbb43741\nparent 968bcb47d0ca0e2659309a30a69c400a828980ca\nauthor renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1789717016 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789717016 +0800\n\nchore(deps): update all non-major dependencies (#541)\n\n* chore(deps): update all non-major dependencies\n\n* fix(sandbox): drop unused ts-expect-error after modern.js 3.9 bump\n\n* feat(rsbuild-plugin-react-native-web): support reanimated 4 webUtils imports\n\nreanimated 4 ships js-reanimated/webUtils.js as plain ESM that bare-imports\nreact-native-web/dist/cjs/... without declaring react-native-web as a\ndependency, so under pnpm''s isolated node_modules the specifiers cannot be\nresolved from within reanimated''s virtual store. Extend the existing\nwebUtils transform to rewrite those specifiers to absolute paths via\nresolveModule (framework-react-native-web already passes reactNativeWebPath),\nfalling back to untouched code when no resolver is available or throws. The\n3.x webUtils.web.js export-let/try/require transform is unchanged.\n\nAlso upgrade the react-native-web sandbox to react-native-reanimated\n^3.19.5 -> ^4.6.0 (react-native-worklets ^0.12.2). This additionally removes\nthe @babel/types 8.x phantom-dependency crash of reanimated 3''s Babel plugin,\nwhich loaded an undeclared hoisted @babel/types 8.0.4 and threw\n\"NumericLiterals must be non-negative finite numbers\"; worklets 0.12 declares\n@babel/types ^7 so the plugin now resolves a safe 7.x copy.\n\n* revert(rsbuild-plugin-react-native-web): drop reanimated 4 webUtils import rewrite\n\nThe rewrite patched around react-native-reanimated''s undeclared\nreact-native-web dependency at build time; a pnpm-workspace.yaml\nhoistPattern entry now covers it for every bundler instead.\n\n* chore: hoist react-native-web for reanimated 4 and drop worklets babel hoists\n\nreact-native-reanimated 4''s js-reanimated/webUtils.js imports\nreact-native-web/dist/cjs/... without declaring react-native-web as a\ndependency. pnpm''s default hoistPattern [''*''] covers this, but this repo\nrestricts hoistPattern, so add react-native-web to it. Conversely,\nreact-native-worklets 0.12 declares @babel/types, @babel/generator and\n@babel/traverse in its own dependencies, so those hoist entries are no\nlonger needed and are removed.\n\nAlso document the pnpm hoisting requirement in the react-native-web\nframework guide (en + zh).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: fi3ework <fi3ework@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrOoYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAS8QQABsH4GEPDzF9TMCr9qK9IEYv\n6HgZWJIWAYXxhQvE/pJpt0fAmDjocLiG8gf5LeW3MeYMbwZEn+Ifh7S+E2ClxBgN\nl2BrjB9fN/f5Xl2WnozU9zROsyrvD3Lz5QMhyr5z5z0tK0bqAQ1y7DDoeHYY0NzS\nrxBeIq/ooAKC00wvx+cML/LjtqWG2NoNdxkFwHroAZMMwenRyQ9ws7dy0D16mLbp\nc4FR0I241PjzKDAlKXTDKqph208IzQ0lPvrTZHNifwZyenUx76dhvHhr+cF3YTaG\nC4BBnCwtUiruXetzURGtVcoDXlAhsoKbgbUAhLVLkwAmqLAFwG1acgFZhicGcPzl\nivCXduljI/6h2VTWz7iLulWinEUpntEUp2GsIfPdiLc/rR1Wzxi8Folg1yu/lmHp\nd6cKohShIMSGXj0RAgfHIs1sRp6zWUYsgtKOB4yIaijQRGJgnWDNELIfl/3RSo7p\nPylM5kVZ/06vz9MKe359ZNkwgQyb0NhY/Ef5ngrryJQwbfw6GYhE+y82xuKdmVkK\nvWj7QzRkhWwDMnW8zxucmvIlJrWt/pgthApVpfrW++qruXVy/W2F8QNrT2xCZqv+\nWtJdBgJazXFFlw0+Kactn29o6QRB6mdjPHWnW4eUo/EgO3owuRe9Cc5VFl7OPn4S\nb6VeEkWB7yK7pJTzxiV7\n=wDQc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T07:36:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commit/8e7425261266c7ba573da8cabf748b3bc57dabe4","node_id":"C_kwDOL8RLndoAKDhlNzQyNTI2MTI2NmM3YmE1NzNkYThjYWJmNzQ4YjNiYzU3ZGFiZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commit/968bcb47d0ca0e2659309a30a69c400a828980ca","sha":"968bcb47d0ca0e2659309a30a69c400a828980ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/968bcb47d0ca0e2659309a30a69c400a828980ca"}],"sha":"8e7425261266c7ba573da8cabf748b3bc57dabe4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/8e7425261266c7ba573da8cabf748b3bc57dabe4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12322740?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fi3ework","id":12322740,"login":"fi3ework","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzIyNzQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/968bcb47d0ca0e2659309a30a69c400a828980ca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T05:55:14Z","email":"fi3ework@gmail.com","name":"Max"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T05:55:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(addon-modernjs): apply only the browser environment of the Modern.js config (#580)\n\n* fix(addon-modernjs): apply only the client environment of the Modern.js config\n\nModern.js accepts a user-written environments map and merges environments.client\ninto its browser build. The addon forwarded that map verbatim, so a client\nassetPrefix leaked into the Storybook preview unstripped and other environments\nreached Storybook''s Rsbuild config. Merge environments.client over the top-level\nconfig, drop the rest, then strip as before. The e2e leak probe now covers it.\n\n* fix(addon-modernjs): accept Modern.js v2''s web browser environment\n\nModern.js names the browser environment client on v3 and web on v2; the addon\nsupports both majors, so take whichever is present. The e2e leak probe adds a\nweb bait so both the merged-then-stripped and the dropped cases stay covered.","tree":{"sha":"6e49f72638a2b00c530fc0f6e02454b3f38e3b9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/trees/6e49f72638a2b00c530fc0f6e02454b3f38e3b9a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/commits/968bcb47d0ca0e2659309a30a69c400a828980ca","verification":{"payload":"tree 6e49f72638a2b00c530fc0f6e02454b3f38e3b9a\nparent 4939946e6506e6ae00f6a5ed1992f2b4fea8edf1\nauthor Max <fi3ework@gmail.com> 1789710914 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789710914 +0800\n\nfix(addon-modernjs): apply only the browser environment of the Modern.js config (#580)\n\n* fix(addon-modernjs): apply only the client environment of the Modern.js config\n\nModern.js accepts a user-written environments map and merges environments.client\ninto its browser build. The addon forwarded that map verbatim, so a client\nassetPrefix leaked into the Storybook preview unstripped and other environments\nreached Storybook''s Rsbuild config. Merge environments.client over the top-level\nconfig, drop the rest, then strip as before. The e2e leak probe now covers it.\n\n* fix(addon-modernjs): accept Modern.js v2''s web browser environment\n\nModern.js names the browser environment client on v3 and web on v2; the addon\nsupports both majors, so take whichever is present. The e2e leak probe adds a\nweb bait so both the merged-then-stripped and the dropped cases stay covered.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrNJCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjNIQAJsxY/hBepajz12ATp5jsyN8\nf/GH/ZhRh6zjnRI4QBPWNBy1Q6xk4xQmHjMF0L8on/g8Ih/QL8/VVepd5C1ZskII\nTRmXHTUKCbcyOfkBD2EBMr4IDzLMk06sXYfym6Ky/PQIQ+eiUiIeX5KU1xDrEgOs\nJeA3UAjyex3Oubg64kFc3kHM108f0MsG8mh7R2irglQcMXC1fE6HJH5CkrVHuNxl\nVY5ICWYRzzs3U2pZY9u9e6p3B0Anpk6COBi7SWPWOo9BMiHYgBLWf88ktSRsr1+9\nAjFKeJTUqJ7WCLr1iSOvDhz6VW+6tSV+spWWfw9dHJ1GkhoxdIDcbSFueFU/fwt2\nrm7224niQ5LPisuR/i+qEQqLHsxPXLpH8E9tGAdr62owP2CbdQmVITkOlME+/EUZ\nkjqRGQG6C16N2T41++xE3QnXWZw+W3IFf8iWAlbBAn1o0IDSV9oSVbxf7LmjTLfn\n2QzCwtjFf1FHmkokXnpvM4o4y5rR8pCSePBTEMxRKObb0KaTgPKTc1L5p58fhoRa\n0cRRBrlzJP/NHdBF6zxAHyPUug8nGiZeivbOBJu4wQHp4afZ127sZAW/QHv0tY6y\niMJfhJ3YbTi9N0XaFNIQrXAmco0RTPi4a4g+1uyI7Iz7211tvVHTTFYKTcLQNQ2C\nfl5jM9uyMVMywTBadmkb\n=YpQM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T05:55:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commit/968bcb47d0ca0e2659309a30a69c400a828980ca","node_id":"C_kwDOL8RLndoAKDk2OGJjYjQ3ZDBjYTBlMjY1OTMwOWEzMGE2OWM0MDBhODI4OTgwY2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commit/4939946e6506e6ae00f6a5ed1992f2b4fea8edf1","sha":"4939946e6506e6ae00f6a5ed1992f2b4fea8edf1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/4939946e6506e6ae00f6a5ed1992f2b4fea8edf1"}],"sha":"968bcb47d0ca0e2659309a30a69c400a828980ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/968bcb47d0ca0e2659309a30a69c400a828980ca"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12322740?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fi3ework","id":12322740,"login":"fi3ework","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzIyNzQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/4939946e6506e6ae00f6a5ed1992f2b4fea8edf1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T09:07:41Z","email":"fi3ework@gmail.com","name":"Max"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T09:07:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(addon-rstack): load app and lib config from rstack.config.* (#579)\n\n* feat(addon-rstack): load app and lib config from rstack.config.*\n\nAdd storybook-addon-rstack so projects on Rstack CLI can reuse their\n`define.app()` / `define.lib()` definitions in the Storybook preview\nwithout keeping a duplicate rslib.config.* or copying settings into\n.storybook/main.ts.\n\n- Load definitions through the public `rstack/config` loader, resolve\n  function-form definitions with Storybook-derived params, prefer app\n  and fall back to lib unless `configType` is set.\n- Share environment selection + stripping between the builder and the\n  addon via `resolveInheritedRsbuildConfig` in storybook-builder-rsbuild.\n  An explicit `environment` name that does not exist now throws even\n  when the config has zero or one environment.\n- Extract `resolveLibRsbuildConfig` from storybook-addon-rslib; the new\n  addon bundles it as a devDependency instead of depending on @rslib/core.\n- Bump the root `rstack` devDependency to 0.7.4 and drop five type\n  assertions its typed lint flags as redundant.\n- Add the rstack-react-component sandbox with an e2e spec, and bilingual\n  integration docs.\n\nCloses #571\n\n* docs(addon-rstack): type-check the main.ts examples with twoslash\n\n* docs(addon-rstack): use typed StorybookConfig in main.ts examples\n\n* docs(addon-rslib): use typed StorybookConfig in main.ts examples\n\n* refactor(addon-rstack): drop the redundant cwd option\n\nconfigFilePath alone locates the config (absolute, or relative to the\ncurrent working directory), matching the builder''s rsbuildConfigPath and\naddon-modernjs''s configPath.\n\n* refactor(addon-rstack): select the definition through a stack option\n\nReplace the flat configType/environment/libIndex options with a\ndiscriminated `stack` option: `{ type: ''app'', environment? }` or\n`{ type: ''lib'', libIndex? }`. App-only and lib-only settings can no\nlonger be combined, and the option is open to more definition types.\nOmitting `stack` keeps app-first auto selection.\n\nFunction-form definitions now receive the same params Rsbuild''s own\nconfig loader builds (`command` from `process.argv[2]`), instead of an\naddon-specific mapping from Storybook''s configType, so the behavior\nmatches storybook-addon-rslib and needs no extra documentation.\n\n* refactor(addon-rstack): resolve the selected definition on one path\n\nPick the definition first and throw when it is missing, resolve the\nfunction form once, and branch only at the resolver. Narrow\nresolveLibRsbuildConfig to the options it reads and make the source\nlabel required instead of defaulting to the Rslib wording.\n\nDrop the mock-based params test that the real-loader fixture already\ncovers, the unused define.test() in that fixture, and the duplicate\nempty-environments case in the unknown-name matrix.\n\n* test(addon-rstack): cover define.app() with the rstack-react sandbox\n\nThe sandbox inherited an async define.lib(), which is the same path the\nrslib-react-component sandbox already covers end to end. Turn it into a\nReact app that inherits an async define.app() so the environment\nselection path runs against the real Rstack loader in e2e, and rename\nit to rstack-react. Extract expectDocsTitle for the docs assertion.\n\n* refactor(addon-rslib): resolve lib config through the environment helper\n\nAn Rslib lib entry is merged over the top-level config the same way\nRsbuild merges an environment, so select lib[i] as a one-entry\nenvironments map and let resolveInheritedRsbuildConfig do the merge\nand the strip. Rslib never reads a user-written top-level\nenvironments key, so it is dropped instead of being selected.\n\n* chore(addon-rstack): drop leftovers flagged by the simplify pass\n\nFlatten the lib entry lookup in resolveLibRsbuildConfig, remove the\nsandbox source.entry that only restated the Rsbuild default and\ntriggered a strip warning on every Storybook start, and drop the\noutDir left over from the library sandbox.\n\n* refactor: rename the config helpers and strip at each call site\n\n- resolveInheritedRsbuildConfig -> pickRsbuildEnvironment: merges the selected\n  environment over the top-level config and no longer strips\n- resolveLibRsbuildConfig -> rslibConfigToRsbuildConfig: converts an Rslib\n  config into one lib entry''s Rsbuild config; modifyLibRsbuildConfig moves to\n  the addon preset so it still runs after stripping\n- builder, addon-rslib and addon-rstack call stripInheritedConfig explicitly,\n  matching addon-modernjs\n\n* refactor: drop the fake lib environment and the one-caller e2e helper\n\n- rslibConfigToRsbuildConfig merges lib[i] over the shared config directly;\n  routing it through pickRsbuildEnvironment only reached one branch\n- pickRsbuildEnvironment selects with environment ?? names[0]\n- inline expectDocsTitle into the rstack-react spec, matching the other specs\n- drop the forked type-check from the rstack-react sandbox\n- trim a duplicate invalid-name case and name the addon tests by behavior\n\n* test(addon-rstack): cover define.lib() with the rstack-react-component sandbox\n\n- restore the async define.lib() sandbox as sandboxes/rstack-react-component\n  (React + Sass plugins, esm/cjs lib entries) and register its e2e on port 6114\n- export CounterButtonProps so the standalone rstack lib build can emit dts\n- link both Rstack examples from the docs\n\n* chore(sandboxes): trim the rstack-react-component sandbox to what it demonstrates\n\n- one bundleless esm lib entry plus plugins, mirroring rslib-vue3-component;\n  dts, the cjs entry and the entry glob never reached Storybook\n- drop dist entry fields and redundant tsconfig compilerOptions in both\n  Rstack sandboxes (root tsconfig already sets strict, jsx and noEmit)","tree":{"sha":"4bee51d48c4a27ca8cf9ffab3f92d4ee840fb850","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/trees/4bee51d48c4a27ca8cf9ffab3f92d4ee840fb850"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/commits/4939946e6506e6ae00f6a5ed1992f2b4fea8edf1","verification":{"payload":"tree 4bee51d48c4a27ca8cf9ffab3f92d4ee840fb850\nparent f16ec7db1bb81d000282c3952c8a5244b6696710\nauthor Max <fi3ework@gmail.com> 1789636061 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789636061 +0800\n\nfeat(addon-rstack): load app and lib config from rstack.config.* (#579)\n\n* feat(addon-rstack): load app and lib config from rstack.config.*\n\nAdd storybook-addon-rstack so projects on Rstack CLI can reuse their\n`define.app()` / `define.lib()` definitions in the Storybook preview\nwithout keeping a duplicate rslib.config.* or copying settings into\n.storybook/main.ts.\n\n- Load definitions through the public `rstack/config` loader, resolve\n  function-form definitions with Storybook-derived params, prefer app\n  and fall back to lib unless `configType` is set.\n- Share environment selection + stripping between the builder and the\n  addon via `resolveInheritedRsbuildConfig` in storybook-builder-rsbuild.\n  An explicit `environment` name that does not exist now throws even\n  when the config has zero or one environment.\n- Extract `resolveLibRsbuildConfig` from storybook-addon-rslib; the new\n  addon bundles it as a devDependency instead of depending on @rslib/core.\n- Bump the root `rstack` devDependency to 0.7.4 and drop five type\n  assertions its typed lint flags as redundant.\n- Add the rstack-react-component sandbox with an e2e spec, and bilingual\n  integration docs.\n\nCloses #571\n\n* docs(addon-rstack): type-check the main.ts examples with twoslash\n\n* docs(addon-rstack): use typed StorybookConfig in main.ts examples\n\n* docs(addon-rslib): use typed StorybookConfig in main.ts examples\n\n* refactor(addon-rstack): drop the redundant cwd option\n\nconfigFilePath alone locates the config (absolute, or relative to the\ncurrent working directory), matching the builder''s rsbuildConfigPath and\naddon-modernjs''s configPath.\n\n* refactor(addon-rstack): select the definition through a stack option\n\nReplace the flat configType/environment/libIndex options with a\ndiscriminated `stack` option: `{ type: ''app'', environment? }` or\n`{ type: ''lib'', libIndex? }`. App-only and lib-only settings can no\nlonger be combined, and the option is open to more definition types.\nOmitting `stack` keeps app-first auto selection.\n\nFunction-form definitions now receive the same params Rsbuild''s own\nconfig loader builds (`command` from `process.argv[2]`), instead of an\naddon-specific mapping from Storybook''s configType, so the behavior\nmatches storybook-addon-rslib and needs no extra documentation.\n\n* refactor(addon-rstack): resolve the selected definition on one path\n\nPick the definition first and throw when it is missing, resolve the\nfunction form once, and branch only at the resolver. Narrow\nresolveLibRsbuildConfig to the options it reads and make the source\nlabel required instead of defaulting to the Rslib wording.\n\nDrop the mock-based params test that the real-loader fixture already\ncovers, the unused define.test() in that fixture, and the duplicate\nempty-environments case in the unknown-name matrix.\n\n* test(addon-rstack): cover define.app() with the rstack-react sandbox\n\nThe sandbox inherited an async define.lib(), which is the same path the\nrslib-react-component sandbox already covers end to end. Turn it into a\nReact app that inherits an async define.app() so the environment\nselection path runs against the real Rstack loader in e2e, and rename\nit to rstack-react. Extract expectDocsTitle for the docs assertion.\n\n* refactor(addon-rslib): resolve lib config through the environment helper\n\nAn Rslib lib entry is merged over the top-level config the same way\nRsbuild merges an environment, so select lib[i] as a one-entry\nenvironments map and let resolveInheritedRsbuildConfig do the merge\nand the strip. Rslib never reads a user-written top-level\nenvironments key, so it is dropped instead of being selected.\n\n* chore(addon-rstack): drop leftovers flagged by the simplify pass\n\nFlatten the lib entry lookup in resolveLibRsbuildConfig, remove the\nsandbox source.entry that only restated the Rsbuild default and\ntriggered a strip warning on every Storybook start, and drop the\noutDir left over from the library sandbox.\n\n* refactor: rename the config helpers and strip at each call site\n\n- resolveInheritedRsbuildConfig -> pickRsbuildEnvironment: merges the selected\n  environment over the top-level config and no longer strips\n- resolveLibRsbuildConfig -> rslibConfigToRsbuildConfig: converts an Rslib\n  config into one lib entry''s Rsbuild config; modifyLibRsbuildConfig moves to\n  the addon preset so it still runs after stripping\n- builder, addon-rslib and addon-rstack call stripInheritedConfig explicitly,\n  matching addon-modernjs\n\n* refactor: drop the fake lib environment and the one-caller e2e helper\n\n- rslibConfigToRsbuildConfig merges lib[i] over the shared config directly;\n  routing it through pickRsbuildEnvironment only reached one branch\n- pickRsbuildEnvironment selects with environment ?? names[0]\n- inline expectDocsTitle into the rstack-react spec, matching the other specs\n- drop the forked type-check from the rstack-react sandbox\n- trim a duplicate invalid-name case and name the addon tests by behavior\n\n* test(addon-rstack): cover define.lib() with the rstack-react-component sandbox\n\n- restore the async define.lib() sandbox as sandboxes/rstack-react-component\n  (React + Sass plugins, esm/cjs lib entries) and register its e2e on port 6114\n- export CounterButtonProps so the standalone rstack lib build can emit dts\n- link both Rstack examples from the docs\n\n* chore(sandboxes): trim the rstack-react-component sandbox to what it demonstrates\n\n- one bundleless esm lib entry plus plugins, mirroring rslib-vue3-component;\n  dts, the cjs entry and the entry glob never reached Storybook\n- drop dist entry fields and redundant tsconfig compilerOptions in both\n  Rstack sandboxes (root tsconfig already sets strict, jsx and noEmit)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqq63dCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArMIQAJc+5CllnW5svuqWp1VfDfkh\n+rseQS2GXRkXKjBo4JD16BHLrW0+ne/E41/rgNkr8rsYCXkOU778/FymU6zhpmiV\n+FnIwOxytnnpAeR7jNVYkAu6xm8/v+mbnpqE1fFoQsCltvLGir0wZKMlgSDtZP1Z\np3OkD3CsFEeshTXpGc16e4hu8sQwsSQTM+ahI5be5+gdSvL6ZHT43uQkHC0zOdLQ\nkNmbBvMnYDO6M071a7njiI0CS8MV69d8hPRS5/gcRWTHok5I03sp/e89KDvDi7CZ\n+9/8bKLLmcFT3HRoAMfFC0TlRRHCphcuPXVzuNQfVngd1fVG5cqNGgCoWRzzqfjI\nEfkQtt53dNvlaoKd6VWRn6AeeJvDmWqWt0S3g6ulJ0cm6+A6NLx4Zqz6x7tYd4nB\nkNuWTU2rzUYPpKLBhw95JZ3AFNBjzePko/7N0O7J2mkR61/NASLHfsV5jvCFDE0K\nZPl6gXStUG++efrvv7lzwhgeNSUfWhPZwZ6BKsYkvsiVz3H7flSHoEODsVoDpBbG\n/GpDEzABdHT40kuQCh4mTO5SkURzNkeOe6H+HlOfNVIUUQD0TA2fxE3ZmY2iXqat\nyBiMHygJfI4/29wNBwJjhOBievmmlgC3Cw9