d-lint divergences\n\nRecord String(error) interpolation in the mock runtime warning.\nRecord the unbound-method disable before the HTML hook lookup.\nRecord the unbound-method disable before preset apply destructuring.\nCorrect the comment describing files outside the typed scope.\n\n* chore(lint): type-check tests/, e2e/ and scripts/\n\nAdd per-directory tsconfigs and root Node types, and stop ignoring scripts.\nLoad Node types explicitly for e2e and allow script TypeScript import extensions.\nUse a boolean SHA validator and remove a redundant error assertion.","tree":{"sha":"a4cd56882a8bee0e7f512242b749ba2a82eb7e8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/trees/a4cd56882a8bee0e7f512242b749ba2a82eb7e8f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/commits/473ef922eab13499e8cda7522f92ff1696fdd05f","verification":{"payload":"tree a4cd56882a8bee0e7f512242b749ba2a82eb7e8f\nparent cab8a98176723d3055fdb502fc955555c3153cd5\nauthor Max <fi3ework@gmail.com> 1789471742 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789471742 +0800\n\nchore(lint): enable type-aware linting, replace check-package with rs check --type-check (#570)\n\n* chore(lint): enable type-aware linting, replace check-package with rs check --type-check\n\n* chore(website): keep @shikijs/transformers current, expect the shiki type mismatch\n\nExpect the transformer type mismatch between Shiki types 4.4.x and the 4.3.x resolved by Rspress instead of pinning transformers.\n\nRemove the directives once Rspress resolves shiki 4.4+ and the transformer types align.\n\n* chore(builder-rsbuild): keep upstream''s destructured preset apply\n\nUse an inline unbound-method disable to preserve the upstream preset call shape.\n\n* chore(manifest): record remaining typed-lint divergences\n\nRecord String(error) interpolation in the mock runtime warning.\nRecord the unbound-method disable before the HTML hook lookup.\nRecord the unbound-method disable before preset apply destructuring.\nCorrect the comment describing files outside the typed scope.\n\n* chore(lint): type-check tests/, e2e/ and scripts/\n\nAdd per-directory tsconfigs and root Node types, and stop ignoring scripts.\nLoad Node types explicitly for e2e and allow script TypeScript import extensions.\nUse a boolean SHA validator and remove a redundant error assertion.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqSv+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAT4UQAH6uv898xp1PWoopOn5ftr1A\nEWVfyG3yM+pG1G4I5QXOaBcffa5Q5r/37FwldOwcO0+LE0KVrnpVOYuqV+p1kbG4\nC8F7WJmdAITURiwOpa0QPQvAz2SHid+4pDAstzCaR+ydqMPPUI6jPSYRa0WyLzJq\n+7idg05w0PEQT4kTHtxANeL7N9RJBRfWM1eTPU16ZuDxcBTQWk38OgA1NUq18gm2\n3DExL8wnwe1z0s8LXYnh62Qf9YbemedLPBrugC8NmDvPVbQ4HvsVxw01u7k+oAH6\ncqXapRyiVlIk6NMGlKpZxe4yjB05h+0cYK7AdcQpjwHBY6FOmQSXb5Ql6p8FAzUF\n6i/UGek4lGtVtJeY2ylgRHRBtOvgRzABYGC5oW98ffE9U+IJkQQlKq0xX5UsJE3Q\nBkXAp675rqx5mfQnIDPCTc04FxctHVhV0bxNjblGlOaft2JeLmLk9Hg3pS0VqJv2\nJJmpz93BnT/R19TqecPmUKqtrcP2hdt3Mu+Ce4cWak+CrhK4NTHHgAdJe/VKL8LX\ncoD+mm5PcAtQnL6F9xTxbFvuzXiq75fV7yuP5Est9cr+OUgn9xWppiVXLjGjU/1j\nc9gXhqK9W0dQJ3AliDJHtASHQ7IQKrv1nHS0yECMxRr1PXI/AcNadz9KgS/jJLxa\npRIMNUb/Fub6c8sTj5FZ\n=Reko\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T11:29:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commit/473ef922eab13499e8cda7522f92ff1696fdd05f","node_id":"C_kwDOL8RLndoAKDQ3M2VmOTIyZWFiMTM0OTllOGNkYTc1MjJmOTJmZjE2OTZmZGQwNWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commit/cab8a98176723d3055fdb502fc955555c3153cd5","sha":"cab8a98176723d3055fdb502fc955555c3153cd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/cab8a98176723d3055fdb502fc955555c3153cd5"}],"sha":"473ef922eab13499e8cda7522f92ff1696fdd05f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/473ef922eab13499e8cda7522f92ff1696fdd05f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12322740?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fi3ework","id":12322740,"login":"fi3ework","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzIyNzQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/cab8a98176723d3055fdb502fc955555c3153cd5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T09:29:29Z","email":"fi3ework@gmail.com","name":"Max"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T09:29:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(website): derive peer dependency ranges from package manifests (#574)\n\n* docs(website): derive peer dependency ranges from package manifests\n\nThe docs hard-coded `storybook >= 10.0.0` / `@rsbuild/core >= 1.0.1`, while\nthe real peer ranges are pinned to the Storybook renderers'' peers and move on\nevery bump (`^10.6.0` today). Add an Rsbuild plugin that expands\n`<PeerRange name=\"...\" />` in `.mdx` into inline code read from\n`packages/*/package.json` at build time, applied to the HTML, `.md` and\nllms.txt outputs alike, so Storybook bumps no longer require doc edits.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013BDTYog94uwq5p2LDM9Pzc\n\n* refactor(website): expand PeerRange with Rspress replaceRules\n\nDrop the custom Rsbuild transform plugin: Rspress applies `replaceRules` to\nthe raw source before compiling MDX for every output, so a handful of rules\nbuilt in `rstack.config.ts` do the same job with no extra file, and the\nwebsite tsconfig type-checks them. Source the ranges from `framework-react`\n(whose peers `pnpm check-dependency-version` cross-checks) instead of the\nbuilder, which that check exempts. Tighten the docs wording to what the\nmechanism guarantees.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013BDTYog94uwq5p2LDM9Pzc\n\n* chore(website): satisfy CodeQL incomplete-sanitization on pipe escaping\n\n`range.replace(/\\|/g, ''\\\\|'')` trips `js/incomplete-sanitization` even though\nthe input is a semver range from our own manifests. `split(''|'').join(''\\\\|'')`\nis equivalent and not flagged.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013BDTYog94uwq5p2LDM9Pzc\n\n* refactor(website): make PeerRange a theme component fed by source.define\n\nReplace the `replaceRules` text substitution with a real `<PeerRange />`\ncomponent exported from `@theme`. The ranges are still read from the package\nmanifests in `rstack.config.ts`, now injected as `__PEER_RANGES__` through\nRsbuild `source.define`. The `.md` / llms.txt pipeline renders only top-level\nJSX and prints components nested in Markdown tables or lists as literal text,\nso the requirement tables become JSX tables and the info block uses\nparagraphs with the component inline. Verified HTML, per-page `.md` and\n`llms-full.txt` all show the real ranges.\n\n* fix(website): render peer range unions without literal pipes\n\n`renderToMarkdown` serializes code spans verbatim, so a union such as\n`^1.5.0 || ^2.0.0-0` inside a GFM table cell split the requirements table in\nthe `.md` / llms.txt outputs. Render one code span per alternative joined by\n` / ` instead, which is valid in every output.\n\n* fix(website): pass peer ranges through verbatim, escape pipes only in md cells\n\nRender the manifest range as-is instead of splitting unions. Table usages\npass `cell`, and only the `.md` / llms.txt build (Rspress defines\n`__SSR_MD__` for its `node_md` environment) escapes `|` there, which GFM\nrequires even inside code spans; prose keeps the literal range in every\noutput.","tree":{"sha":"c16b0ff18bd9029d654ed82eac823f0f06502361","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/trees/c16b0ff18bd9029d654ed82eac823f0f06502361"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/commits/cab8a98176723d3055fdb502fc955555c3153cd5","verification":{"payload":"tree c16b0ff18bd9029d654ed82eac823f0f06502361\nparent dc6a179e36cb3212301980876d48a147d70778a9\nauthor Max <fi3ework@gmail.com> 1788859769 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788859769 +0800\n\ndocs(website): derive peer dependency ranges from package manifests (#574)\n\n* docs(website): derive peer dependency ranges from package manifests\n\nThe docs hard-coded `storybook >= 10.0.0` / `@rsbuild/core >= 1.0.1`, while\nthe real peer ranges are pinned to the Storybook renderers'' peers and move on\nevery bump (`^10.6.0` today). Add an Rsbuild plugin that expands\n`<PeerRange name=\"...\" />` in `.mdx` into inline code read from\n`packages/*/package.json` at build time, applied to the HTML, `.md` and\nllms.txt outputs alike, so Storybook bumps no longer require doc edits.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013BDTYog94uwq5p2LDM9Pzc\n\n* refactor(website): expand PeerRange with Rspress replaceRules\n\nDrop the custom Rsbuild transform plugin: Rspress applies `replaceRules` to\nthe raw source before compiling MDX for every output, so a handful of rules\nbuilt in `rstack.config.ts` do the same job with no extra file, and the\nwebsite tsconfig type-checks them. Source the ranges from `framework-react`\n(whose peers `pnpm check-dependency-version` cross-checks) instead of the\nbuilder, which that check exempts. Tighten the docs wording to what the\nmechanism guarantees.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013BDTYog94uwq5p2LDM9Pzc\n\n* chore(website): satisfy CodeQL incomplete-sanitization on pipe escaping\n\n`range.replace(/\\|/g, ''\\\\|'')` trips `js/incomplete-sanitization` even though\nthe input is a semver range from our own manifests. `split(''|'').join(''\\\\|'')`\nis equivalent and not flagged.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013BDTYog94uwq5p2LDM9Pzc\n\n* refactor(website): make PeerRange a theme component fed by source.define\n\nReplace the `replaceRules` text substitution with a real `<PeerRange />`\ncomponent exported from `@theme`. The ranges are still read from the package\nmanifests in `rstack.config.ts`, now injected as `__PEER_RANGES__` through\nRsbuild `source.define`. The `.md` / llms.txt pipeline renders only top-level\nJSX and prints components nested in Markdown tables or lists as literal text,\nso the requirement tables become JSX tables and the info block uses\nparagraphs with the component inline. Verified HTML, per-page `.md` and\n`llms-full.txt` all show the real ranges.\n\n* fix(website): render peer range unions without literal pipes\n\n`renderToMarkdown` serializes code spans verbatim, so a union such as\n`^1.5.0 || ^2.0.0-0` inside a GFM table cell split the requirements table in\nthe `.md` / llms.txt outputs. Render one code span per alternative joined by\n` / ` instead, which is valid in every output.\n\n* fix(website): pass peer ranges through verbatim, escape pipes only in md cells\n\nRender the manifest range as-is instead of splitting unions. Table usages\npass `cell`, and only the `.md` / llms.txt build (Rspress defines\n`__SSR_MD__` for its `node_md` environment) escapes `|` there, which GFM\nrequires even inside code spans; prose keeps the literal range in every\noutput.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqn9V5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlQsQAJ1+qsItT3/FzETzXFQCHLI2\n3PbyfMQTqgm7QknXH9p6PahWpy4amh2JHnZzkLvCdHXD88+5PtrDFPEMKdNoczWl\nHrPFqXKpc1PPxY8HtDfEWTpbEPI3Y+CEHMMAdoUQ6gIb3kqpm5GHSgX3Kfqe41D+\n8/nauSroS0S9+sw4vHdalmBZAXECvxATAz0Admwulx65rxVnF4RnV5rfCKslC26P\nlVEEQa1PyO0EgRBBvoaylcXSDi6Wj2lYZ3TdDHR5pRopmIbDbvEJRsST+HpZ9HNT\ncBWI+nIEzqq5GJGH5W6onu6HogefVBNV4HbwakhIajvVlv82D4JQvgmmR/XPV5ua\n903vMfJI2CW0WGKNR5fLAJ9VCRf+2oYpuLTAhkL+/OmAXj1oa2IAFRBZsjUE7Th6\nZ81d6iYwMZmY0z/7ZYKalKU0mvc4lGkX/N5Bo096zixFSQ/vMCI5kiforDyGiyeJ\n8LubYMGjD32foIngJTnFD7jkaEmRfQN5oHTwD5tvT1zyg6wv2UkDBvEEna3hSGC7\nPEjMfDHtwDK4DFwlgtXIIroMvSj+BQUbS6De7YWgOXNouMlB10jyXjEIszRN6krK\nY3lEs4/kCYHMFfo2Gq4cacpfRDy1irRXdbQde17wFOvzDyyc4oqMs15u9qyPWrvN\nBQ7/WJEAOp/0N119Yusn\n=e5gd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T09:29:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-fl