l_url":"https://github.com/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commit/8efba352d2b2202aaef891d660b93178aa98129a","sha":"8efba352d2b2202aaef891d660b93178aa98129a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/8efba352d2b2202aaef891d660b93178aa98129a"}],"sha":"fdc217d48854ffef4d09224c5f8183baf512cca1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/fdc217d48854ffef4d09224c5f8183baf512cca1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12322740?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fi3ework","id":12322740,"login":"fi3ework","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzIyNzQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/8efba352d2b2202aaef891d660b93178aa98129a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T05:33:58Z","email":"fi3ework@gmail.com","name":"Max"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T05:33:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(builder-rsbuild): follow up on the mocker runtime injection fix (#533)\n\n* docs(builder-rsbuild): mark the two upstream divergences in the mocker runtime plugin\n\nBoth edits to this plugin in #531 look like drift when read against Storybook''s\nwebpack5 builder, and both would be undone by a well-meaning sync:\n\n- Upstream reads only `getHooks`. Rspack''s native `HtmlRspackPlugin` dropped that\n  deprecated alias in v2, so `html.implementation: ''native''` needs\n  `getCompilationHooks`.\n- Upstream still keeps the tag `unshift` inside the emit guard, which leaves every\n  HTML page after the first without the runtime. Upstream cannot see it because its\n  preview emits a single `iframe.html`.\n\nComments only, no behaviour change.\n\n* refactor(builder-rsbuild): read `NormalModuleReplacementPlugin` from the compiler\n\nTaking it off the module-level `rspack` namespace forced the test to swap the\nconstructor on that shared export and put it back in a `finally`, which leaks\ninto anything else running in the same process. Upstream''s webpack5 builder\nreads it from the compiler; do the same, and let the stub compiler supply a\nrecorder instead.\n\nAlso drops `process.env.STORYBOOK_DISABLE_TELEMETRY` from the test. It never\ndid anything: `extractMockCalls` does call `telemetry(''mocking'', ...)`, but\n`telemetry()` gates on `globalThis.SB_TELEMETRY_STATE` and never reads that\nvariable. Unset, as it is under test, every event is parked on\n`globalThis.SB_TELEMETRY_QUEUE` and never sent. Replaced with a comment\nrecording why nothing escapes.\n\n* test(builder-rsbuild): pin which hooks accessor the html plugin is read through\n\nThe suite covered a plugin exposing `getCompilationHooks` alone, `getHooks`\nalone, and neither, but not both at once — which is what html-rspack-plugin\nexports behind the default `html.implementation: ''js''`, and what rspack v1\nexports too. That is the path nearly every build takes, and nothing said which\nof the two names it goes through.\n\nGive each accessor its own hooks object so the stub can report the route taken,\nand assert the current name wins. Flipping the `??` operands in the plugin\nfails this test and only this test.","tree":{"sha":"1ccfb0a63cce5beb645ede5babc6f26419a09a6a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/trees/1ccfb0a63cce5beb645ede5babc6f26419a09a6a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/commits/8efba352d2b2202aaef891d660b93178aa98129a","verification":{"payload":"tree 1ccfb0a63cce5beb645ede5babc6f26419a09a6a\nparent 14d1a82d2aa5f61914b09af18e6114a4881e5552\nauthor Max <fi3ework@gmail.com> 1786426438 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786426438 +0800\n\nrefactor(builder-rsbuild): follow up on the mocker runtime injection fix (#533)\n\n* docs(builder-rsbuild): mark the two upstream divergences in the mocker runtime plugin\n\nBoth edits to this plugin in #531 look like drift when read against Storybook''s\nwebpack5 builder, and both would be undone by a well-meaning sync:\n\n- Upstream reads only `getHooks`. Rspack''s native `HtmlRspackPlugin` dropped that\n  deprecated alias in v2, so `html.implementation: ''native''` needs\n  `getCompilationHooks`.\n- Upstream still keeps the tag `unshift` inside the emit guard, which leaves every\n  HTML page after the first without the runtime. Upstream cannot see it because its\n  preview emits a single `iframe.html`.\n\nComments only, no behaviour change.\n\n* refactor(builder-rsbuild): read `NormalModuleReplacementPlugin` from the compiler\n\nTaking it off the module-level `rspack` namespace forced the test to swap the\nconstructor on that shared export and put it back in a `finally`, which leaks\ninto anything else running in the same process. Upstream''s webpack5 builder\nreads it from the compiler; do the same, and let the stub compiler supply a\nrecorder instead.\n\nAlso drops `process.env.STORYBOOK_DISABLE_TELEMETRY` from the test. It never\ndid anything: `extractMockCalls` does call `telemetry(''mocking'', ...)`, but\n`telemetry()` gates on `globalThis.SB_TELEMETRY_STATE` and never reads that\nvariable. Unset, as it is under test, every event is parked on\n`globalThis.SB_TELEMETRY_QUEUE` and never sent. Replaced with a comment\nrecording why nothing escapes.\n\n* test(builder-rsbuild): pin which hooks accessor the html plugin is read through\n\nThe suite covered a plugin exposing `getCompilationHooks` alone, `getHooks`\nalone, and neither, but not both at once — which is what html-rspack-plugin\nexports behind the default `html.implementation: ''js''`, and what rspack v1\nexports too. That is the path nearly every build takes, and nothing said which\nof the two names it goes through.\n\nGive each accessor its own hooks object so the stub can report the route taken,\nand assert the current name wins. Flipping the `??` operands in the plugin\nfails this test and only this test.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqerRGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAe1YQAD1WlbLQFVkRvD4AphdzeN0I\nGS975POOmEIG+5P2+1+6MQVnzXmI1LA+mIV0VUbsGpa+zks2BPKGU5RnxfYDgRQ4\njcMrL1wUF5R4fm0oC3P36qANNnC86pD2Ou3phVNqCrin4mLhfNzb9tDc8a10EExE\nF5Sl4vafKjhUK5mEze6cXg1H+PDLjbf2VMV8nh1uggdTCfXeIwg1AMVWIemBkP7l\nhnyvVbEdY+eH7FoSit76X40okIwuFd4JRNjpm2/khSCQy4FvI8h76+mPIYXwRh0T\np+yJhNfwse/5X4med4YYcp2yKKdk5Fg4pv9DJO96vq2EvD5f2y/0ov3aA0WBHOoO\nSI5/UR6zjQkteltDU0lv9X5SgjWAYp+VFO16iHLciw+OsTlOxJsVE5Fju4mkr5Z5\npnXvkBWQYT6txUNl1hB6XOWv65dAMcyz5i3w+p1SoiVOjpqdLHbgAwcuVqJWPAj7\ncmjuD0+I0A9nmc1FBHzEYxHrlFq9L8TrrFPsg1XQeZDQoCz6WloAZIdCUiK/vOpu\nvgjShQTS3rl2iOCdBmvYm7akkxNXHda4EcAyxvmV0keEG1ggQM1BweFzEHS3EouO\nQMLZHGMd77C40VxzA1xeQtg22ew9/E+2Xzcg2TVuG1fGvz+6gwWsgDgBxuFtW6GC\nvUrwcFz4cuW8gqhIbdDc\n=0Isg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-11T05:46:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commit/8efba352d2b2202aaef891d660b93178aa98129a","node_id":"C_kwDOL8RLndoAKDhlZmJhMzUyZDJiMjIwMmFhZWY4OTFkNjYwYjkzMTc4YWE5ODEyOWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commit/14d1a82d2aa5f61914b09af18e6114a4881e5552","sha":"14d1a82d2aa5f61914b09af18e6114a4881e5552","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/14d1a82d2aa5f61914b09af18e6114a4881e5552"}],"sha":"8efba352d2b2202aaef891d660b93178aa98129a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/8efba352d2b2202aaef891d660b93178aa98129a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8297838?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Codex-/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Codex-/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Codex-/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Codex-/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Codex-","id":8297838,"login":"Codex-","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgyOTc4Mzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Codex-/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Codex-/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Codex-/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Codex-/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Codex-/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Codex-","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/14d1a82d2aa5f61914b09af18e6114a4881e5552/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T03:36:52Z","email":"codex.nz@gmail.com","name":"Alex Miller"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T03:36:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(builder-rsbuild): repair mocker runtime injection (#531)\n\n* test(builder-rsbuild): cover `RspackMockPlugin` resolution and caching\n\n`RspackMockPlugin` shipped without tests. Pin the behaviour that is easy to\nregress silently: the early return when no mocks are declared, and the mtime\ncache, including the equality comparison that makes restoring an older preview\nconfig invalidate the map where a \"newer than\" check would not.\n\n* fix(builder-rsbuild): reference the mocker runtime from every HTML page\n\n`beforeAssetTagGeneration` runs once per HTML page, each with its own asset\nlist, but the emit guard also gated the tag. The first page got the runtime and\nevery later page silently went without it, so mocks never installed there.\n\nGuard only the emit, which is all the rebuild loop it was added for needs, and\nprepend the tag unconditionally.\n\n* fix(builder-rsbuild): handle deprecated `HtmlPlugin` api usage\n\nRspack''s native HtmlRspackPlugin exposes `getCompilationHooks` and no\n`getHooks`, so looking only for the deprecated name meant the mocker runtime was\nnever injected there, with nothing but a warning to say so. Resolve whichever of\nthe two the plugin offers, preferring the current name, and bail only when\nneither is present. Both are plain statics that ignore `this`, so the extracted\nfunction is safe to call unbound.\n\n* test(builder-rsbuild): cover mocker runtime injection\n\nDrives the plugin against a stub compiler whose HTML plugin exposes each hooks\napi in turn, and runs the tag hook once per page to record what that page ends up\nreferencing.\n\nBoth fixes are pinned. Against the previous code the `getCompilationHooks` path\nfails outright, and with only the tag guard put back the second page comes back\nwith no scripts at all.\n\n* test(builder-rsbuild): resolve expected mock redirect with pathe\n\n* test(builder-rsbuild): cast the mock plugin compiler stub via unknown","tree":{"sha":"d089aa7f86b3cdaca19e96598c944905c9c0cd4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/trees/d089aa7f86b3cdaca19e96598c944905c9c0cd4c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/commits/14d1a82d2aa5f61914b09af18e6114a4881e5552","verification":{"payload":"tree d089aa7f86b3cdaca19e96598c944905c9c0cd4c\nparent 26c459519f09ba830489cffb641d5c48c51cfe9b\nauthor Alex Miller <codex.nz@gmail.com> 1786419412 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786419412 +0800\n\nfix(builder-rsbuild): repair mocker runtime injection (#531)\n\n* test(builder-rsbuild): cover `RspackMockPlugin` resolution and caching\n\n`RspackMockPlugin` shipped without tests. Pin the behaviour that is easy to\nregress silently: the early return when no mocks are declared, and the mtime\ncache, including the equality comparison that makes restoring an older preview\nconfig invalidate the map where a \"newer than\" check would not.\n\n* fix(builder-rsbuild): reference the mocker runtime from every HTML page\n\n`beforeAssetTagGeneration` runs once per HTML page, each with its own asset\nlist, but the emit guard also gated the tag. The first page got the runtime and\nevery later page silently went without it, so mocks never installed there.\n\nGuard only the emit, which is all the rebuild loop it was added for needs, and\nprepend the tag unconditionally.\n\n* fix(builder-rsbuild): handle deprecated `HtmlPlugin` api usage\n\nRspack''s native HtmlRspackPlugin exposes `getCompilationHooks` and no\n`getHooks`, so looking only for the deprecated name meant the mocker runtime was\nnever injected there, with nothing but a warning to say so. Resolve whichever of\nthe two the plugin offers, preferring the current name, and bail only when\nneither is present. Both are plain statics that ignore `this`, so the extracted\nfunction is safe to call unbound.\n\n* test(builder-rsbuild): cover mocker runtime injection\n\nDrives the plugin against a stub compiler whose HTML plugin exposes each hooks\napi in turn, and runs the tag hook once per page to record what that page ends up\nreferencing.\n\nBoth fixes are pinned. Against the previous code the `getCompilationHooks` path\nfails outright, and with only the tag guard put back the second page comes back\nwith no scripts at all.\n\n* test(builder-rsbuild): resolve expected mock redirect with pathe\n\n* test(builder-rsbuild): cast the mock plugin compiler stub via unknown","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqepjUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnY0QAEqoGxlqQYWf/8Zbl/9IpJcQ\nba0X2c895ua7DyXIziFRzL6UvHVuqqK2Ewqa4X1iro0+JjfH676bb9IBeXVB8kxP\nDGbg1zLmmYH68rK69qCUGZgqxdsl8OcxCpJCxBEWJmBTA0ORaS8MhAgU5P3cLNsH\nNREGVrt0eGePbUAzd10CW6+ZQQWaFkXm/0QA0a3h0uxMKGsTNdU4tqkXr62CxFX3\nmSLurT5zu93EhYNvKXmtulWVd0tx7d8J2K+PRbzsRMS88iA8DNJtQUSDBHFA8LeA\n54C4Km3bsgOXVlyb+fLNiYgPOhkJqxGQRzpArhtq7rgg850yglA+EYskEx7MLJXD\nQnReon1Dlh75Feq/6jj/2zQ9WJUQjEXutA3RXgmQ01UMTLxU2noJZWvoYCBwqUtD\n387Xf/CQiIvqFIICmfCPCmgfKdz+rBK/G0eTNlGsd/RJne/sMTUJQOMVYEb0+yiy\nCq8gn0JE/LCENEsFuKsr8FyRKFBGovfOLHkXD641QFw+9jcLrMAfTOJcRDGQ/8S6\nilEfmOyv0s8Kq9WfF6YSnGNCjlbMH84kIj90ThLUrUjMq0ZlanQPyPfe/qdDuDJD\nSiOoXjUomDIEMLWjxE6vSJ+rDtiRAWoqhPUzlkn4fIKUPjO4/HPbKLAbdoE+jK+p\nmce5jBFSspmwBswRzA37\n=eKjg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-11T04:53:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/f