torybook-rsbuild/commits/5666ad8a491d1deeabe7ad3425c20f2c87e03548"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12322740?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fi3ework","id":12322740,"login":"fi3ework","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzIyNzQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/eda227f7953e9b544fea3f290b85e26a085d7d88/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T08:54:05Z","email":"fi3ework@gmail.com","name":"fi3ework"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T08:54:05Z","email":"fi3ework@gmail.com","name":"fi3ework"},"message":"chore: narrow the packages workspace glob to packages/*\n\n`packages/**` matched packages/builder-rsbuild/compiled/@storybook/core-webpack,\nwhich prebundle emits with a real package.json. pnpm treated that build artifact\nas a workspace member, so every `pnpm install` added a spurious\n\n  packages/builder-rsbuild/compiled/@storybook/core-webpack: {}\n\nimporter entry to pnpm-lock.yaml, dirtying the working tree.\n\nAll ten real packages live directly under packages/, so `packages/*` covers them.\n`sandboxes/**` keeps its recursive glob — sandboxes/modernjs-react-mf/host and\n/remote are genuinely nested.","tree":{"sha":"fa32f1588f63b0ee1c00ff8700b649f13f9be97a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/trees/fa32f1588f63b0ee1c00ff8700b649f13f9be97a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/commits/eda227f7953e9b544fea3f290b85e26a085d7d88","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12322740?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fi3ework","id":12322740,"login":"fi3ework","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzIyNzQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commit/eda227f7953e9b544fea3f290b85e26a085d7d88","node_id":"C_kwDOL8RLndoAKGVkYTIyN2Y3OTUzZTliNTQ0ZmVhM2YyOTBiODVlMjZhMDg1ZDdkODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commit/e8bd7e19c110256a3c6c699a03774654b7a2d60e","sha":"e8bd7e19c110256a3c6c699a03774654b7a2d60e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/e8bd7e19c110256a3c6c699a03774654b7a2d60e"}],"sha":"eda227f7953e9b544fea3f290b85e26a085d7d88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/eda227f7953e9b544fea3f290b85e26a085d7d88"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12322740?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fi3ework","id":12322740,"login":"fi3ework","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzIyNzQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/e8bd7e19c110256a3c6c699a03774654b7a2d60e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T07:20:35Z","email":"fi3ework@gmail.com","name":"Max"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T07:20:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: port 6 high-severity behaviors missing from the upstream Storybook port (#528)\n\n* fix(framework-react): restore docgen fallbacks missing from the port\n\nThree behaviors present in upstream Storybook never made it into this\npackage. Found by a full-content drift audit against\nstorybookjs/storybook@next (3e12dfc040).\n\n- The `typescriptPresent` probe was computed but its `if` body was empty,\n  so the react-docgen-typescript plugin loaded unconditionally. Since\n  `typescript` is an optional peerDependency and the vendored plugin\n  imports it dynamically, a JS-only project setting\n  `reactDocgen: ''react-docgen-typescript''` failed at startup instead of\n  degrading. Upstream gates the plugin on the same condition and falls\n  back to plain react-docgen (react-vite/src/preset.ts, 01e3663b76).\n\n- Under the react-docgen-typescript backend, .js/.jsx/.mjs/.cjs files got\n  no docgen at all: the vendored plugin only matches `**/**.tsx`. Upstream\n  mounts an additional react-docgen loader on /\\.(cjs|mjs|jsx?)$/ inside\n  the same branch (presets/react-webpack/src/framework-preset-react-docs.ts).\n  Extracted `reactDocgenLoaderRule(test)` so both branches share one\n  wiring; the two filters partition cleanly.\n\n- tsconfig lookup tried only `tsconfig.json`. In monorepos and Vite-style\n  React apps that keep `tsconfig.base.json` or `tsconfig.app.json` at the\n  root, `matchPath` stayed undefined and prop tables for aliased imports\n  came out empty. Ported the fallback chain from 07edf14e (fixes upstream\n  issue 24585). Upstream''s loader emits no warnings on this path, so none\n  are added here.\n\nNote: when the guard fails, the fallback include here is\n/\\.(cjs|mjs|tsx?|jsx?)$/ rather than upstream-vite''s /\\.(mjs|jsx?)$/,\nwhich would leave .ts/.tsx with no docgen at all. Upstream''s webpack side\nagrees with the wider form.\n\n* fix(builder-rsbuild): add storybook resolve conditions, fix blocks external\n\nTwo behaviors present in upstream Storybook never made it into the\npreview config. Found by a full-content drift audit against\nstorybookjs/storybook@next (3e12dfc040).\n\n- `resolve.conditionNames` was never set, so a dependency shipping a\n  `storybook`, `stories` or `test` export condition silently resolved to\n  its default entry and its mock/test variant never loaded. Upstream adds\n  these in preview/base-webpack.config.ts (3ff3e13bf, part of module\n  mocking) and builder-vite does the same in storybook-config-plugin.ts,\n  so this is a cross-builder contract rather than a webpack quirk. The\n  trailing ''...'' is the sentinel that re-inserts the default conditions\n  instead of replacing them; verified @rspack/core expands it in\n  `cleverMerge` on both the 1.x and 2.x peer ranges.\n\n- `build.test.disableBlocks` externalized `@storybook/blocks`, a package\n  that no longer exists: it was folded into `@storybook/addon-docs/blocks`\n  upstream in 75df3c88e (SB9). Docs blocks were therefore bundled into\n  --test builds anyway, and the paired `__STORYBOOK_BLOCKS_EMPTY_MODULE__`\n  global was dead. The old key is dropped rather than kept alongside: this\n  package peers on storybook@^10.5.3, so no supported dependency can\n  import it. Resolves the stale \"remove in v3 (SB10)\" TODO.\n\n* fix(framework-html): re-export StorybookConfig from the /node entrypoint\n\n`defineMain()` is exported from `storybook-html-rsbuild/node` but\n`StorybookConfig` was not, so TypeScript could not name the return type\nand users hit \"type cannot be named\" in main.ts. Upstream fixed this in\n4ae17109; framework-react, framework-vue3 and framework-web-components\nalready carry the re-export, so this was an isolated port miss. All four\nnode entrypoints are now identical.\n\nFound by a full-content drift audit against\nstorybookjs/storybook@next (3e12dfc040).","tree":{"sha":"9d93b655d9d15eee469df7aa2584d05019b22bac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/trees/9d93b655d9d15eee469df7aa2584d05019b22bac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/commits/e8bd7e19c110256a3c6c699a03774654b7a2d60e","verification":{"payload":"tree 9d93b655d9d15eee469df7aa2584d05019b22bac\nparent 078aa25171ae7ceedd4091efb4253a6325fa0a38\nauthor Max <fi3ework@gmail.com> 1785741635 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785741635 +0000\n\nfix: port 6 high-severity behaviors missing from the upstream Storybook port (#528)\n\n* fix(framework-react): restore docgen fallbacks missing from the port\n\nThree behaviors present in upstream Storybook never made it into this\npackage. Found by a full-content drift audit against\nstorybookjs/storybook@next (3e12dfc040).\n\n- The `typescriptPresent` probe was computed but its `if` body was empty,\n  so the react-docgen-typescript plugin loaded unconditionally. Since\n  `typescript` is an optional peerDependency and the vendored plugin\n  imports it dynamically, a JS-only project setting\n  `reactDocgen: ''react-docgen-typescript''` failed at startup instead of\n  degrading. Upstream gates the plugin on the same condition and falls\n  back to plain react-docgen (react-vite/src/preset.ts, 01e3663b76).\n\n- Under the react-docgen-typescript backend, .js/.jsx/.mjs/.cjs files got\n  no docgen at all: the vendored plugin only matches `**/**.tsx`. Upstream\n  mounts an additional react-docgen loader on /\\.(cjs|mjs|jsx?)$/ inside\n  the same branch (presets/react-webpack/src/framework-preset-react-docs.ts).\n  Extracted `reactDocgenLoaderRule(test)` so both branches share one\n  wiring; the two filters partition cleanly.\n\n- tsconfig lookup tried only `tsconfig.json`. In monorepos and Vite-style\n  React apps that keep `tsconfig.base.json` or `tsconfig.app.json` at the\n  root, `matchPath` stayed undefined and prop tables for aliased imports\n  came out empty. Ported the fallback chain from 07edf14e (fixes upstream\n  issue 24585). Upstream''s loader emits no warnings on this path, so none\n  are added here.\n\nNote: when the guard fails, the fallback include here is\n/\\.(cjs|mjs|tsx?|jsx?)$/ rather than upstream-vite''s /\\.(mjs|jsx?)$/,\nwhich would leave .ts/.tsx with no docgen at all. Upstream''s webpack side\nagrees with the wider form.\n\n* fix(builder-rsbuild): add storybook resolve conditions, fix blocks external\n\nTwo behaviors present in upstream Storybook never made it into the\npreview config. Found by a full-content drift audit against\nstorybookjs/storybook@next (3e12dfc040).\n\n- `resolve.conditionNames` was never set, so a dependency shipping a\n  `storybook`, `stories` or `test` export condition silently resolved to\n  its default entry and its mock/test variant never loaded. Upstream adds\n  these in preview/base-webpack.config.ts (3ff3e13bf, part of module\n  mocking) and builder-vite does the same in storybook-config-plugin.ts,\n  so this is a cross-builder contract rather than a webpack quirk. The\n  trailing ''...'' is the sentinel that re-inserts the default conditions\n  instead of replacing them; verified @rspack/core expands it in\n  `cleverMerge` on both the 1.x and 2.x peer ranges.\n\n- `build.test.disableBlocks` externalized `@storybook/blocks`, a package\n  that no longer exists: it was folded into `@storybook/addon-docs/blocks`\n  upstream in 75df3c88e (SB9). Docs blocks were therefore bundled into\n  --test builds anyway, and the paired `__STORYBOOK_BLOCKS_EMPTY_MODULE__`\n  global was dead. The old key is dropped rather than kept alongside: this\n  package peers on storybook@^10.5.3, so no supported dependency can\n  import it. Resolves the stale \"remove in v3 (SB10)\" TODO.\n\n* fix(framework-html): re-export StorybookConfig from the /node entrypoint\n\n`defineMain()` is exported from `storybook-html-rsbuild/node` but\n`StorybookConfig` was not, so TypeScript could not name the return type\nand users hit \"type cannot be named\" in main.ts. Upstream fixed this in\n4ae17109; framework-react, framework-vue3 and framework-web-components\nalready carry the re-export, so this was an isolated port miss. All four\nnode entrypoints are now identical.\n\nFound by a full-content drift audit against\nstorybookjs/storybook@next (3e12dfc040).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcEFDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQJUQAHWMioeWh7I9XsdIUuDIv9zb\nHub3/R7kaO5/K9WJ9B/ZFXd3a/HZEN2ICL7PvdDIsohqcHTPUSpGUjNLqv7OrpuY\nwPHzpMJa7OsU1YXUCjPXkzoC3uuYySihGCsEM+QGjr3/ej2Gy/aoXWoUBzqUkFL9\n32e0jUx3F3LXJJLPOjtHoJr6JvCzNEM3sgJQ9/3JAgjzclnUJZmun3RCDw8pni0F\nJd8INDCfhwZXThfZEaKWCPA/94HwjgAux0ZGgyo4T9ooMj0TWhR1oXc5+vspeKjT\nAq1yjuzJMXi2V3V3XyYeW+EsZ0IyfjvCDRAGsfDS5ustrdW/KK5i99YqGf1cNz0W\nt+bKznsBsr3KYLiN1dY28S+7IXrxBbwuf0rroFKNv3ZCYaB8qEeUgboo6B1/9D5+\ntyR8lzzeDOJHGd1N60MOTHYkYQX55O5OqI8SBSBljix