rivacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commit/b9b1f79ec8f43d6db1ae27a1de1665aaba4b4f84","node_id":"C_kwDOL8RLndoAKGI5YjFmNzllYzhmNDNkNmRiMWFlMjdhMWRlMTY2NWFhYmE0YjRmODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commit/27d68823b60ba52d956c94411835faf7aa9e0db9","sha":"27d68823b60ba52d956c94411835faf7aa9e0db9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/27d68823b60ba52d956c94411835faf7aa9e0db9"}],"sha":"b9b1f79ec8f43d6db1ae27a1de1665aaba4b4f84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/b9b1f79ec8f43d6db1ae27a1de1665aaba4b4f84"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12322740?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fi3ework","id":12322740,"login":"fi3ework","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzIyNzQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/27d68823b60ba52d956c94411835faf7aa9e0db9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T05:55:06Z","email":"fi3ework@gmail.com","name":"Max"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T05:55:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(skill): add storybook-check drift audit, harden storybook-sync triage (#527)\n\n* chore(skill): add storybook-check drift audit, harden storybook-sync triage\n\nstorybook-sync consumes the upstream commit stream incrementally, so\nevery commit gets exactly one triage judgment and is never revisited -\na structural blind spot when a judgment is wrong.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. New storybook-check skill: a stateless, full-sweep drift audit.\n   A file-level manifest maps upstream builder and framework sources\n   (builder-webpack5, react-webpack5/react-vite, presets/react-webpack,\n   vue3-vite, web-components-vite, html-vite) to their ported local\n   counterparts, with accepted intentional divergences recorded per\n   entry. Every run first validates the mapping itself against both\n   repos (coverage: unmapped/missing files on either side), then audits\n   content one subagent per local package - the axis the ports converge\n   on, since several upstream packages can feed one local package.\n   No cursors: unresolved drift re-surfaces on every run by\n   construction. The plumbing is dependency-free Node, run directly\n   with node - no build step, so it works from a bare checkout.\n\n2. storybook-sync hardening: a skip verdict of \"no Rsbuild parallel\"\n   is gated on a counterpart lookup in the shared manifest (file\n   granularity) and on actually reading the local file, both in direct\n   analysis and in the subagent prompt. The package mapping table is\n   scoped to commit watching only, and the watch scope covers every\n   port source the manifest maps - including code/frameworks/html-vite\n   and code/presets/react-webpack, the verbatim origin of\n   framework-react''s react-docgen-loader.\n\n* chore: remove committed drift-check report\n\n* fix(skill): exclude entries without an upstream path from the coverage sweep\n\nvalidateManifest already reports them as INVALID-MANIFEST, but the sweep\nthen called srcDir(undefined) and crashed before printing any findings -\nexactly in the malformed-manifest scenario coverage exists to diagnose.\n\n* fix(skill): harden coverage against Windows separators, record CDA divergence\n\n- Normalize local sweep paths to forward slashes before comparing with\n  manifest entries, which are always slash-separated; on Windows join()\n  produces backslashes and every mapped file misreported as\n  UNLISTED-LOCAL.\n- Record the change-detection adapter''s graph-based add-vs-change\n  classification as an intentional divergence so full sweeps stop\n  re-surfacing it as an undocumented finding.","tree":{"sha":"33c4758e0aa2de8ac150b1a6b1ae3f267d4d912f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/trees/33c4758e0aa2de8ac150b1a6b1ae3f267d4d912f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/commits/27d68823b60ba52d956c94411835faf7aa9e0db9","verification":{"payload":"tree 33c4758e0aa2de8ac150b1a6b1ae3f267d4d912f\nparent 3bca346d83dfbc9ab43dd6ba6a0736d7129c43d8\nauthor Max <fi3ework@gmail.com> 1785736506 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785736506 +0800\n\nchore(skill): add storybook-check drift audit, harden storybook-sync triage (#527)\n\n* chore(skill): add storybook-check drift audit, harden storybook-sync triage\n\nstorybook-sync consumes the upstream commit stream incrementally, so\nevery commit gets exactly one triage judgment and is never revisited -\na structural blind spot when a judgment is wrong.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. New storybook-check skill: a stateless, full-sweep drift audit.\n   A file-level manifest maps upstream builder and framework sources\n   (builder-webpack5, react-webpack5/react-vite, presets/react-webpack,\n   vue3-vite, web-components-vite, html-vite) to their ported local\n   counterparts, with accepted intentional divergences recorded per\n   entry. Every run first validates the mapping itself against both\n   repos (coverage: unmapped/missing files on either side), then audits\n   content one subagent per local package - the axis the ports converge\n   on, since several upstream packages can feed one local package.\n   No cursors: unresolved drift re-surfaces on every run by\n   construction. The plumbing is dependency-free Node, run directly\n   with node - no build step, so it works from a bare checkout.\n\n2. storybook-sync hardening: a skip verdict of \"no Rsbuild parallel\"\n   is gated on a counterpart lookup in the shared manifest (file\n   granularity) and on actually reading the local file, both in direct\n   analysis and in the subagent prompt. The package mapping table is\n   scoped to commit watching only, and the watch scope covers every\n   port source the manifest maps - including code/frameworks/html-vite\n   and code/presets/react-webpack, the verbatim origin of\n   framework-react''s react-docgen-loader.\n\n* chore: remove committed drift-check report\n\n* fix(skill): exclude entries without an upstream path from the coverage sweep\n\nvalidateManifest already reports them as INVALID-MANIFEST, but the sweep\nthen called srcDir(undefined) and crashed before printing any findings -\nexactly in the malformed-manifest scenario coverage exists to diagnose.\n\n* fix(skill): harden coverage against Windows separators, record CDA divergence\n\n- Normalize local sweep paths to forward slashes before comparing with\n  manifest entries, which are always slash-separated; on Windows join()\n  produces backslashes and every mapped file misreported as\n  UNLISTED-LOCAL.\n- Record the change-detection adapter''s graph-based add-vs-change\n  classification as an intentional divergence so full sweeps stop\n  re-surfacing it as an undocumented finding.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcC07CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcYUQAHffv/Tyz97MXfTB0kUGJDlC\nP3CArcCOM2a9IoMfEXE4pQLhcmynGUPxBoVKbCt38Bl1txRKteENyweg9DKDp8SV\nnPgKTwCjyN3Lbd7fEvcyAkA2yPFTIlcWYzPSRkaJmGBLyNV9IJKlBn8XeWz7Mmvc\np9rxaR446k7QizyISTdMIOl5L+VTW3rmcZ7fG+9yNDW+olMKVyah/aDzs6ZDwMB3\nMhPEjdnwz/f0+Z7fuaLiJeneJPFNZ+ETWkTVPHWAVIcFysV7gT2cfqt+lDaaPdWI\nL3c3v/QyEGE8x28OjSxNgFOCb3BnStjaiFGGekpZNXkmjmy7qEg9HH5mPLFohgLp\nI4/QdNou3wCu9z+V6Z0H0w3UWFGxA7ogjF+vQ7LOvBYsoFTvU9DZUVzM+iUXWu1O\n7AmWrjvXwiNwLnptui6ybC3Wej/CyzMVr6Ey/te7eRS03baqn2wiyfbbATTvBOen\nB962uLnN40GalNFcmvGimQKKuasanBhD6DckP+/fbWZY86FwGSIuVqeUEDBv+jEN\nMUHhh2WURPUzaYRnWgavzAjhbeto/vYACTdbERvCrkftO0qzlGJu9EfYWJzEJwlp\n3Lj5HN2J3DYVIPnIqWnGIowBzr53Vrn+GoNgW6/O0YF2PugblT20RGKg7K8HTQZB\ncwP2SUUZFYEd1jliRX62\n=U0nE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-03T05:55:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_adm