"2026-07-31T08:50:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(builder-rsbuild): skip mock resolution probe when no mocks are declared (#524)\n\n* fix(builder-rsbuild): skip mock resolution probe when no mocks are declared\n\nRspackMockPlugin registers a NormalModuleReplacementPlugin matching every\nmodule request and resolves each one via resolveWithExtensions/\nresolveExternalModule before checking the mock map, even when zero\nsb.mock() calls exist. On builds with many modules this adds a\nsignificant, entirely wasted resolution cost to every build.\n\nThe webpack5 builder had the identical issue (storybookjs/storybook#33778)\nand already ships the fix (storybookjs/storybook#33169): skip resolution\nentirely when the mock map is empty, pre-filter external specifiers\nagainst a candidate set, and cache the mock map by the preview config''s\nmtime instead of rebuilding it on every run. This ports the same fix to\nRspackMockPlugin, keeping the existing Windows path-normalization and\nconfigDir handling specific to this package.\n\n* fix(builder-rsbuild): use strict mtime equality for mock cache reuse\n\n<= treated a preview config mtime moving backward (e.g. git checkout to\nan older commit, a restored backup) as \"unchanged\", silently reusing a\nstale mockMap/candidateSpecifiers. Only an exact match means the file\nis genuinely the same as last observed.\n\nAddresses review feedback on #524.\n\n* fix(builder-rsbuild): cache mocker runtime and emit it once per compilation\n\nRspackInjectMockerRuntimePlugin regenerated the mocker runtime and\nunconditionally re-emitted `mocker-runtime-injected.js` on every\ncompilation, even though the content never changes. Re-emitting an\nidentical asset triggers spurious rebuild loops in dev.\n\nThis is the second half of storybookjs/storybook#33169, which fixed the\nidentical issue in WebpackInjectMockerRuntimePlugin: cache the runtime\nstring on the plugin instance, and guard the emit + `data.assets.js`\nunshift behind a `compilation.getAsset()` check so both happen once.\n\n* docs(builder-rsbuild): flag the canonicalized specifier gap in the mock pre-filter\n\n`candidateSpecifiers` is built from `mock.path`, but `extractMockCalls` strips\nthe extension from that value when the declared specifier''s basename matches the\nresolved file''s basename. `sb.mock(''pkg/dist/index.js'')` is therefore stored as\n`pkg/dist/index` while `resource.request` keeps the `.js`, so the external\npre-filter misses the request and skips the mock with no error.\n\nRecord it in place rather than fix it here. builder-webpack5 carries the same\nbug on `next`.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: fi3ework <fi3ework@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"92c917ae190d20d8106bf43afae48152a34e9671","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/trees/92c917ae190d20d8106bf43afae48152a34e9671"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/commits/700bd71a85b39f8cc3abec0ddaa515c033e1938b","verification":{"payload":"tree 92c917ae190d20d8106bf43afae48152a34e9671\nparent 9108e6087c667b15a89cda19025713af1e14b9ab\nauthor benwarbrooke-auror <ben.warbrooke@auror.co> 1785487800 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785487800 +0000\n\nfix(builder-rsbuild): skip mock resolution probe when no mocks are declared (#524)\n\n* fix(builder-rsbuild): skip mock resolution probe when no mocks are declared\n\nRspackMockPlugin registers a NormalModuleReplacementPlugin matching every\nmodule request and resolves each one via resolveWithExtensions/\nresolveExternalModule before checking the mock map, even when zero\nsb.mock() calls exist. On builds with many modules this adds a\nsignificant, entirely wasted resolution cost to every build.\n\nThe webpack5 builder had the identical issue (storybookjs/storybook#33778)\nand already ships the fix (storybookjs/storybook#33169): skip resolution\nentirely when the mock map is empty, pre-filter external specifiers\nagainst a candidate set, and cache the mock map by the preview config''s\nmtime instead of rebuilding it on every run. This ports the same fix to\nRspackMockPlugin, keeping the existing Windows path-normalization and\nconfigDir handling specific to this package.\n\n* fix(builder-rsbuild): use strict mtime equality for mock cache reuse\n\n<= treated a preview config mtime moving backward (e.g. git checkout to\nan older commit, a restored backup) as \"unchanged\", silently reusing a\nstale mockMap/candidateSpecifiers. Only an exact match means the file\nis genuinely the same as last observed.\n\nAddresses review feedback on #524.\n\n* fix(builder-rsbuild): cache mocker runtime and emit it once per compilation\n\nRspackInjectMockerRuntimePlugin regenerated the mocker runtime and\nunconditionally re-emitted `mocker-runtime-injected.js` on every\ncompilation, even though the content never changes. Re-emitting an\nidentical asset triggers spurious rebuild loops in dev.\n\nThis is the second half of storybookjs/storybook#33169, which fixed the\nidentical issue in WebpackInjectMockerRuntimePlugin: cache the runtime\nstring on the plugin instance, and guard the emit + `data.assets.js`\nunshift behind a `compilation.getAsset()` check so both happen once.\n\n* docs(builder-rsbuild): flag the canonicalized specifier gap in the mock pre-filter\n\n`candidateSpecifiers` is built from `mock.path`, but `extractMockCalls` strips\nthe extension from that value when the declared specifier''s basename matches the\nresolved file''s basename. `sb.mock(''pkg/dist/index.js'')` is therefore stored as\n`pkg/dist/index` while `resource.request` keeps the `.js`, so the external\npre-filter misses the request and skips the mock with no error.\n\nRecord it in place rather than fix it here. builder-webpack5 carries the same\nbug on `next`.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: fi3ework <fi3ework@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbGG4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAsMQAKq9Sl1acRFbpGSfexm9a9g8\nt