ers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commit/e79f4f96f0bb493b6445144580295bf6de7a0e1f","node_id":"C_kwDOL8RLndoAKGU3OWY0Zjk2ZjBiYjQ5M2I2NDQ1MTQ0NTgwMjk1YmY2ZGU3YTBlMWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commit/d592958775c66dc046a4721ff76514841fc3874b","sha":"d592958775c66dc046a4721ff76514841fc3874b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/d592958775c66dc046a4721ff76514841fc3874b"}],"sha":"e79f4f96f0bb493b6445144580295bf6de7a0e1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/e79f4f96f0bb493b6445144580295bf6de7a0e1f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12322740?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fi3ework","id":12322740,"login":"fi3ework","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzIyNzQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi3ework","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/commits/d592958775c66dc046a4721ff76514841fc3874b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T06:38:41Z","email":"fi3ework@gmail.com","name":"Max"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T06:38:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(builder-rsbuild): exclude node_modules from the stories require.context (#506)\n\n* fix(builder-rsbuild): exclude node_modules from the stories require.context\n\nStorybook core''s generated `webpackInclude` carries a `(?!.*node_modules)`\nguard, but it''s unanchored (core strips the leading `^`), so it only keeps\n`node_modules` out because webpack''s `require.context` already drops candidates\nresolved under `resolve.modules` (its default `RequireContextPlugin` rewrites\nthem to bare specifiers and hides the relative form).\n\nRspack''s `ContextModule` has no such rewrite, so it enumerates `node_modules`\nand the guard no-ops. A dependency that ships `.stories.*` files under a folder\nthe glob matches (e.g. its own `src/`) then gets swept into the preview build —\nunder the next-rspack bridge the file hits `next-swc-loader`''s node_modules\nexclude and the build fails with an opaque parse error.\n\nRe-assert the intent by injecting an explicit `webpackExclude: /node_modules/`\n(honored by Rspack for webpack compatibility) into the generated stories\nimportFn, only for the guarded includes — a glob that intentionally targets\nnode_modules (no guard emitted by core) is left untouched.\n\n* fix(builder-rsbuild): avoid ReDoS in node_modules story-context exclusion\n\nCodeQL flagged the comment-spanning regex (two `.*` around the\n`(?!.*node_modules)` literal, run with `gm` on the generated module that\nembeds user-controlled story globs) as polynomial-backtracking ReDoS.\n\nReplace it with plain line-by-line string scanning: a line gets the\n`webpackExclude: /node_modules/` comment only when it contains both\n`webpackInclude:` and the `(?!.*node_modules)` guard. No regex, linear time,\nsame behavior.\n\n* test(builder-rsbuild): type stories-context options as Options instead of never\n\n* fix(builder-rsbuild): anchor node_modules story-context exclude to path separators\n\nA bare `webpackExclude: /node_modules/` is a substring match against each\ncandidate''s absolute path, so it also prunes first-party stories when the\nproject is checked out under a directory whose name merely contains\n`node_modules` (e.g. `/builds/node_modules-cache/app/`), yielding an empty\nstories module. Anchor it to path separators — `/[\\\\/]node_modules[\\\\/]/` —\nwhich still excludes real dependency stories while leaving such paths intact.\n\nAdd a regression test and a TODO referencing the upstream Rspack root-cause fix\n(web-infra-dev/rspack#14576).\n\n* fix(builder-rsbuild): exclude node_modules even when a glob contains the substring\n\nGate the webpackExclude injection on a real [\\/]node_modules[\\/] path\nsegment in the generated webpackInclude, not on core''s (?!.*node_modules)\nguard. Core suppresses that guard for any glob whose string merely contains\nthe node_modules substring (e.g. @(src|node_modules-cache)/**), which would\notherwise leave that context''s dependency sweep unguarded.\n\n* test(builder-rsbuild): add node_modules-sweep regression to react-18 sandbox\n\nRoot the react-18 sandbox stories glob with a brace alternation\n(`../@(modules|src)/**`) whose `modules` branch matches the\n`node_modules` path segment. Under Rspack this makes `require.context`\nenumerate node_modules and sweep `@storybook/react`''s shipped\n`template/cli/**` stories into the preview build, which fails to resolve\ntheir `.css`/`.jsx` siblings — verified the build breaks without the\nbuilder fix and passes with it. `pnpm build:sandboxes` now guards #506.\n\n* fix(builder-rsbuild): decide node_modules exclude from the structured glob\n\nCodex review flagged that an intentional grouped/alternation stories glob\n(e.g. `{ directory: ''./@(src|node_modules)'', files: ''**/*.stories.tsx'' }`)\nwas wrongly stripped: core emits its include as `(src|node_modules)` with\nno literal `/node_modules/` segment, so the previous line-level segment test\nmissed it and injected the exclude — pruning the very dependency stories the\nuser asked for. The webpack builder surfaces those (core suppresses its\n`(?!.*node_modules)` guard), so we must too.\n\nDecide intent from the SAME structured glob core uses (rebuilt from the\nnormalized `{directory, files}` specifier) instead of pattern-matching the\nemitted regex string, which keeps spawning edge cases. `node_modules` is\nrecognised only as a full path segment or exact alternation branch, so\nsubstring look-alikes (`node_modules-cache`) still get the exclude. Also\ncondenses the over-long doc comment.","tree":{"sha":"8ccc0af8b01a15c26ffe79abbdeafc5571f8788f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/trees/8ccc0af8b01a15c26ffe79abbdeafc5571f8788f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/storybook-rsbuild/git/commits/d592958775c66dc046a4721ff76514841fc3874b","verification":{"payload":"tree 8ccc0af8b01a15c26ffe79abbdeafc5571f8788f\nparent 626924a7b6b5ca3d259655c516eb54356e25a037\nauthor Max <fi3ework@gmail.com> 1782715121 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782715121 +0800\n\nfix(builder-rsbuild): exclude node_modules from the stories require.context (#506)\n\n* fix(builder-rsbuild): exclude node_modules from the stories require.context\n\nStorybook core''s generated `webpackInclude` carries a `(?!.*node_modules)`\nguard, but it''s unanchored (core strips the leading `^`), so it only keeps\n`node_modules` out because webpack''s `require.context` already drops candidates\nresolved under `resolve.modules` (its default `RequireContextPlugin` rewrites\nthem to bare specifiers and hides the relative form).\n\nRspack''s `ContextModule` has no such rewrite, so it enumerates `node_modules`\nand the guard no-ops. A dependency that ships `.stories.*` files under a folder\nthe glob matches (e.g. its own `src/`) then gets swept into the preview build —\nunder the next-rspack bridge the file hits `next-swc-loader`''s node_modules\nexclude and the build fails with an opaque parse error.\n\nRe-assert the intent by injecting an explicit `webpackExclude: /node_modules/`\n(honored by Rspack for webpack compatibility) into the generated stories\nimportFn, only for the guarded includes — a glob that intentionally targets\nnode_modules (no guard emitted by core) is left untouched.\n\n* fix(builder-rsbuild): avoid ReDoS in node_modules story-context exclusion\n\nCodeQL flagged the comment-spanning regex (two `.*` around the\n`(?!.*node_modules)` literal, run with `gm` on the generated module that\nembeds user-controlled story globs) as polynomial-backtracking ReDoS.\n\nReplace it with plain line-by-line string scanning: a line gets the\n`webpackExclude: /node_modules/` comment only when it contains both\n`webpackInclude:` and the `(?!.*node_modules)` guard. No regex, linear time,\nsame behavior.\n\n* test(builder-rsbuild): type stories-context options as Options instead of never\n\n* fix(builder-rsbuild): anchor node_modules story-context exclude to path separators\n\nA bare `webpackExclude: /node_modules/` is a substring match against each\ncandidate''s absolute path, so it also prunes first-party stories when the\nproject is checked out under a directory whose name merely contains\n`node_modules` (e.g. `/builds/node_modules-cache/app/`), yielding an empty\nstories module. Anchor it to path separators — `/[\\\\/]node_modules[\\\\/]/` —\nwhich still excludes real dependency stories while leaving such paths intact.\n\nAdd a regression test and a TODO referencing the upstream Rspack root-cause fix\n(web-infra-dev/rspack#14576).\n\n* fix(builder-rsbuild): exclude node_modules even when a glob contains the substring\n\nGate the webpackExclude injection on a real [\\/]node_modules[\\/] path\nsegment in the generated webpackInclude, not on core''s (?!.*node_modules)\nguard. Core suppresses that guard for any glob whose string merely contains\nthe node_modules substring (e.g. @(src|node_modules-cache)/**), which would\notherwise leave that context''s dependency sweep unguarded.\n\n* test(builder-rsbuild): add node_modules-sweep regression to react-18 sandbox\n\nRoot the react-18 sandbox stories glob with a brace alternation\n(`../@(modules|src)/**`) whose `modules` branch matches the\n`node_modules` path segment. Under Rspack this makes `require.context`\nenumerate node_modules and sweep `@storybook/react`''s shipped\n`template/cli/**` stories into the preview build, which fails to resolve\ntheir `.css`/`.jsx` siblings — verified the build breaks without the\nbuilder fix and passes with it. `pnpm build:sandboxes` now guards #506.\n\n* fix(builder-rsbuild): decide node_modules exclude from the structured glob\n\nCodex review flagged that an intentional grouped/alternation stories glob\n(e.g. `{ directory: ''./@(src|node_modules)'', files: ''**/*.stories.tsx'' }`)\nwas wrongly stripped: core emits its include as `(src|node_modules)` with\nno literal `/node_modules/` segment, so the previous line-level segment test\nmissed it and injected the exclude — pruning the very dependency stories the\nuser asked for. The webpack builder surfaces those (core suppresses its\n`(?!.*node_modules)` guard), so we must too.\n\nDecide intent from the SAME structured glob core uses (rebuilt from the\nnormalized `{directory, files}` specifier) instead of pattern-matching the\nemitted regex string, which keeps spawning edge cases. `node_modules` is\nrecognised only as a full path segment or exact alternation branch, so\nsubstring look-alikes (`node_modules-cache`) still get the exclude. Also\ncondenses the over-long doc comment.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQhLxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAARMQAIhXZTDDvLfdQk2B8rGdcfDF\nULebf7Hj811yajTn9pfnRLW1+qKHvlcby+JyVaelz4rkVaHugMqsCOHCkDXe2piM\nXxuLtX6lIuE4XYyYRM9xsNGlVqAUSzFhAkjAD2Qo3eEkfRmtumXXNfX/SQ3zp2lw\nCmIut3OHKEjCaQ+dPNG2ZLec3tJhNRI5K+oKXouEGjq9oO9BoMKTkaf3dzFDZUkP\nsRSi1AMcPP5dmAwyiJMfRnVdOPlDsffcpiQ6L/bryswvwSC6/B58aDn//CRgscjM\nebbjhSK3BVGbNQrOGRMR1AFUZfcSVGviLfmBYtLTrTv3c3x6VUqV9hbwBunKPpiQ\n/CGfRsXDhpb2u6Q/OuuWr9D1LtKAYW93wlsGfymth1c/O+5ueYy735CWNGXMt6Tq\n+MUp1tZbQd4NQ+N8/B/O5kzLh3mbV1iDbsbeXo6JB7YkAcursjdVIbxAKehoaiie\n/djiy1c+ehQoPZFaSwfoH3TM4fZNZDtj9ORFDITcAAeDVczI+w4+cgi8tizH8xdM\nnC6Aqd2RBfR4isDxIV5yXNBhLkwZHdkEE0jsoKUvZrfNM1K/2TRxGVlHVBKiZfIB\n5LXKZa893rJm7DFy99+wgW7buTK4Ab+DeuQ2t23rgq46WR4WGJQNNwbu3sS9/IaW\n2bnP8gWPvNp1FhdJRhy0\n=QL1F\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-29T06:38:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"p