lar/commits/0a1a772f08b2cbc7bf3a5362f47d70cf30727f6d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90477293?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eduardohr-muniz","id":90477293,"login":"eduardohr-muniz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNDc3Mjkz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eduardohr-muniz/go_router_modular/commits/929629a6f7188b34126d518428fdccded8bbddc9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T22:22:15Z","email":"eduardohr.muniz@outlook.com","name":"Eduardo Muniz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T22:22:15Z","email":"eduardohr.muniz@outlook.com","name":"Eduardo Muniz"},"message":"feat: observe the modular runtime through Modular.configure(onTelemetry:)\n\nAdds telemetry as pure observation: one event per change in a module''s\nbind lifecycle (injected, disposed, and the reference kinds, each with\nits trigger, the module instance id and its reference count) and one per\nmessage on the event bus. Events carry toMap() so they drop straight\ninto a Sentry/Crashlytics breadcrumb.\n\nThe listener runs in release too and an exception it throws is\nswallowed, because telemetry must never break a navigation. The bus\nevent carries only the payload''s type name: events routinely hold\npersonal data and telemetry usually leaves the device.\n\ntelemetryFilter decides before the event is built, so what is filtered\nout costs nothing — including naming a module''s binds, the only part\nthat is not O(1).\n\nAlso runs the suite on Chrome in CI, where the hidden-tab and real\nwindow.history tests live, and pins each source-inspection suite to the\nVM (they need dart:io).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4cb542c9f23771ab5d1fbc9d090bfc8c1a63a944","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eduardohr-muniz/go_router_modular/git/trees/4cb542c9f23771ab5d1fbc9d090bfc8c1a63a944"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eduardohr-muniz/go_router_modular/git/commits/929629a6f7188b34126d518428fdccded8bbddc9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90477293?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eduardohr-muniz","id":90477293,"login":"eduardohr-muniz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNDc3Mjkz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eduardohr-muniz/go_router_modular/commit/929629a6f7188b34126d518428fdccded8bbddc9","node_id":"C_kwDOL9LLJ9oAKDkyOTYyOWE2ZjcxODhiMzQxMjZkNTE4NDI4ZmRjY2RlZDhiYmRkYzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eduardohr-muniz/go_router_modular/commit/a3afe50e5113309e26f5d67b411085dc2312ca34","sha":"a3afe50e5113309e26f5d67b411085dc2312ca34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eduardohr-muniz/go_router_modular/commits/a3afe50e5113309e26f5d67b411085dc2312ca34"}],"sha":"929629a6f7188b34126d518428fdccded8bbddc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eduardohr-muniz/go_router_modular/commits/929629a6f7188b34126d518428fdccded8bbddc9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90477293?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eduardohr-muniz","id":90477293,"login":"eduardohr-muniz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNDc3Mjkz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eduardohr-muniz/go_router_modular/commits/a3afe50e5113309e26f5d67b411085dc2312ca34/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T00:08:17Z","email":"eduardohr.muniz@outlook.com","name":"Eduardo Muniz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T00:08:17Z","email":"eduardohr.muniz@outlook.com","name":"Eduardo Muniz"},"message":"fix: mirror the browser history on the page stack and balance module refcounts\n\nOn the web, plain go_router creates one browser history entry per URL change,\nso `context.go(''/b'')` from `/a` left `/a` in the history even though the page\nwas removed from the stack. Pressing back reopened a route that had already\nbeen disposed, and its module came back without binds. Native platforms never\nbehaved that way.\n\n`ModularGoRouter` now swaps in a route information provider that keeps the\nbrowser history mirrored on the page stack: `go` replaces the current entry,\n`push` and nested `go` add one, `pop` steps the browser back and swallows the\nresulting popstate (no re-parse, no guards re-run), and a `go` away from a deep\nstack collapses the history. Pressing forward onto a page that was already\nremoved navigates to its URL as a fresh `go`, so guards, redirects and module\nbinds all run again. A watchdog releases the provider when a requested step\nback never produces a popstate, which would otherwise freeze URL reporting for\ngood. Browser access sits behind `BrowserHistory`, a no-op off the web.\n\nModule reference counting is balanced as well. A module route''s `redirect` runs\non every navigation that passes through it but only creates a page when the\nroute enters the stack, so each redirect now opens at most one pending\nreference, the page claims it from `initState`, and whatever nobody claims\nexpires once the navigation settles. That fixes modules that were never\ndisposed after navigating between sibling routes, after `push`/`pop`, or after\na guard redirected away. A stateful shell no longer unregisters its branch\nmodules, because each branch page already releases its own reference.\n\n`Module.didChangeGoingReference` and `Module.onDidChangeGoingReference` are\ndeprecated and no longer called; reference counting already protects the\n`A -> B -> A` case they guarded. Adds `Modular.resetForTesting()`.\n\nCovered by 19 tests driving a fake browser with session history and popstate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"76849c1c06276fa0b04fbd2f5ee40dc0f50340af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eduardohr-muniz/go_router_modular/git/trees/76849c1c06276fa0b04fbd2f5ee40dc0f50340af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eduardohr-muniz/go_router_modular/git/commits/a3afe50e5113309e26f5d67b411085dc2312ca34","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90477293?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eduardohr-muniz","id":90477293,"login":"eduardohr-muniz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNDc3Mjkz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eduardohr-muniz/go_router_modular/commit/a3afe50e5113309e26f5d67b411085dc2312ca34","node_id":"C_kwDOL9LLJ9oAKGEzYWZlNTBlNTExMzMwOWUyNmY1ZDY3YjQxMTA4NWRjMjMxMmNhMzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eduardohr-muniz/go_router_modular/commit/0d330922e5fdab759c3fa12834f76c05f0a829af","sha":"0d330922e5fdab759c3fa12834f76c05f0a829af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eduard