":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-30T21:53:10Z","email":"90477293+eduardohr-muniz@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Eduardo Muniz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-30T21:53:10Z","email":"90477293+eduardohr-muniz@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Eduardo Muniz"},"message":"## 5.0.6\n\n### Fix\n\n- **Dependency Injection**: Fixed singleton binds being instantiated 3× when a `RouteModule` imports `AppModule` (or any module already registered).\n\n  **Root cause**: `_collectImportedBinds` calls `module.binds(injector)` on every module registration pass, creating new `Bind` objects with `cachedInstance == null`. `commitBatch` correctly skipped those duplicates via the fast-path (`_isSingletonAlreadyRegistered`), but did **not** propagate `cachedInstance` to the new `Bind` object. Downstream methods `_mapBindsToIdentifiers` and `_validateModuleBinds` use `bind.cachedInstance ?? bind.factoryFunction(...)`, so they fell back to calling the factory — executing the constructor 2 extra times.\n\n  **Fix**: when `commitBatch` skips a duplicate bind, it now sets `bind.cachedInstance` from the already-registered bind (`_storage.bindsMap[bind.type]?.cachedInstance`), preventing any further factory calls for that `Bind` object.\n\n- **Dependency Injection**: Fixed orphaned singleton instances when two imported modules declare the same bind type.\n\n  When `Module A` imports both `Module B` and `Module C`, and both declare the same type `Y`, the previous implementation called the factory of `Y_C` even though `Y_B` was already registered (the `_isSingletonAlreadyRegistered` guard fired *after* `_processInstance`). The factory was called, the instance was created and cached in the `Bind` object, but never stored in `bindsMap` — creating a leaked singleton (open streams, duplicate subscriptions, resource conflicts).\n\n  **Fix**: `commitBatch` now checks `_isSingletonAlreadyRegistered` **before** calling `factoryFunction` for typed binds (`bind.type != Object`), completely preventing the duplicate factory call.","tree":{"sha":"97e8f67ee6a5c90a4502a644df1806d488773452","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eduardohr-muniz/go_router_modular/git/trees/97e8f67ee6a5c90a4502a644df1806d488773452"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eduardohr-muniz/go_router_modular/git/commits/86159257573e7bf1d0beff47545e3a381777c177","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90477293?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eduardohr-muniz","id":90477293,"login":"eduardohr-muniz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNDc3Mjkz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eduardohr-muniz","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eduardohr-muniz/go_router_modular/commit/86159257573e7bf1d0beff47545e3a381777c177","node_id":"C_kwDOL9LLJ9oAKDg2MTU5MjU3NTczZTdiZjFkMGJlZmY0NzU0NWUzYTM4MTc3N2MxNzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eduardohr-muniz/go_router_modular/commit/d6626c60ea30a68f23e0c223f01fa172bc06bed3","sha":"d6626c60ea30a68f23e0c223f01fa172bc06bed3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eduardohr-muniz/go_router_modular/commits/d6626c60ea30a68f23e0c223f01fa172bc06bed3"}],"sha":"86159257573e7bf1d0beff