plate project, the pre-configured environment names across all environments actually have type `''DEV'' | ''PRE-PRODUCTION'' | ''''`\n   - the fallback header rendering function `getFallbackHeader` (into which this parameter is sent) doesn’t have such strict type restrictions\n   - it’s perfectly reasonable to allow apps to display something else in the tag\n- updated installation script to patch the DPS home page (used in the fallback prisons header) to point to the “new” url","tree":{"sha":"6ff879b6fc8df330a091d7083ddad60f6e7d3ffd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ministryofjustice/hmpps-connect-dps-components/git/trees/6ff879b6fc8df330a091d7083ddad60f6e7d3ffd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ministryofjustice/hmpps-connect-dps-components/git/commits/7519601dc92567dcfc6b38297d4c0d4be8f43563","verification":{"payload":"tree 6ff879b6fc8df330a091d7083ddad60f6e7d3ffd\nparent c7a5a4fc9368adee08a12effebc0a38ec6ca7029\nauthor ushkarev <ushkarev@users.noreply.github.com> 1781884141 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781884141 +0100\n\nMinor improvements (#183)\n\n- better documentation around how public contract parameters are used\n- relaxed environment name type which was *only* used for display in the fallback header in non-production, we do not need to be strict about the type\n   - “PRODUCTION” is never displayed so shouldn’t need to be expected\n   - in the HMPPS template project, the pre-configured environment names across all environments actually have type `''DEV'' | ''PRE-PRODUCTION'' | ''''`\n   - the fallback header rendering function `getFallbackHeader` (into which this parameter is sent) doesn’t have such strict type restrictions\n   - it’s perfectly reasonable to allow apps to display something else in the tag\n- updated installation script to patch the DPS home page (used in the fallback prisons header) to point to the “new” url","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNWTtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8LUQAC0xe9