ove async flags from component service tests since they’re not needed\n* Add middleware parameter to optionally turn on updating CSP header from MFE response\n* Bump minor-level version because changes should be backwards compatible","tree":{"sha":"2c21cf30452a3ceba8e1888842325e4be8379ff8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ministryofjustice/hmpps-connect-dps-components/git/trees/2c21cf30452a3ceba8e1888842325e4be8379ff8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ministryofjustice/hmpps-connect-dps-components/git/commits/8422872cb3bbb94df9ee059e32ab3b1e175c8e8d","verification":{"payload":"tree 2c21cf30452a3ceba8e1888842325e4be8379ff8\nparent 3d3747d0fa615289e4bb695221848aaf4dea755d\nauthor ushkarev <ushkarev@users.noreply.github.com> 1776156686 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776156686 +0100\n\nCDPS-1906: Set CSP header from MFE-provided directives (#152)\n\n* Merge header/footer “shared data” types into one since MFE api does not distinguish them; the existing exported types remain but are marked as deprecated\n* Update MFE components response type to include new `cspDirectives` property\n* Refactor CSP-updating utility to work with `CspDirectives` type as now returned by MFE /components\n* Ensure `default-src ''self''` Content-Security-Policy directive is present when creating a new header value\n* Update `updateCsp` function signature to pass all options in as one object, maintaining compatibility with previous syntax since it is publicly exposed\n* Update `updateCsp` function to accept custom directives to merge into response\n* Remove async flags from component service tests since they’re not needed\n* Add middleware parameter to optionally turn on updating CSP header from MFE response\n* Bump minor-level version because changes should be backwards compatible","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp3gAOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAG6UQAF6f4dcVLcy4FBua/BC52fEf\nwU2mp/1x7qdUBYQGW+hQuRSGtCFM3gSqVKgjV7Kvq8XdPqC6eLBIKjdQ0v+0Pva5\n